{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MZAR4uLxQr9gGdRYQMSvAK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Observation/containment/resume driver behind ObservedHostTransport.\n2\t\n3\t``ObservedHostDriver.request(argv, *, timeout)`` answers the transport's\n4\tsemantic commands from an injected runner plus explicit callbacks:\n5\t\n6\t* inspect-host: pinned daemon, pinned network and the seven pinned containers\n7\t  through restricted ``--format`` stdout projections to Python, plus both ingress entries and the\n8\t  unknown-writer callback;\n9\t* redis-meta: TYPE/PTTL/LLEN/ZCARD on explicit keys via ``redis-cli`` inside the\n10\t  pinned, label-verified Redis container; no KEYS/SCAN/values/auth in argv, and\n11\t  an auth error is a refusal;\n12\t* block-ingress, ``docker update --restart=no``, ``docker kill --signal=TERM``\n13\t  and ``docker wait`` on the four legacy IDs only;\n14\t* resume (``docker start``, ``docker update --restart=always`` on the four\n15\t  legacy IDs and open-ingress through both bound entries) ONLY when a\n16\t  ``ledger_proof`` bound to this manifest is injected: a fresh read-only\n17\t  PostgreSQL proof (identity, exact baseline ledger, catalog; see\n18\t  first_transition_database.LedgerProof) runs inside every resume request,\n19\t  immediately before its effect. Without it, resume refuses before any call.\n20\t\n21\tEvery other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are\n22\tcallback-reported scope-bound answers, not independent proof, and no token or\n23\tboolean stands for a human approval. Docker values are CLI-reported for an\n24\toperator-configured endpoint; nothing here certifies the host or quiescence.\n25\tReal bindings/manifest values are Phase 3 inputs.\n26\t\n27\tThe Docker CLI applies --format client-side; only its restricted stdout\n28\tprojection enters Python/journals. Tests use synthetic data only.\n29\t\n30\tErrors carry fixed codes only; runner output never enters exceptions, logs or\n31\treceipts. No retry: a timeout or refusal is final for that request. Each\n32\trequest has a cooperative deadline, checked after injected calls return; per-command output caps are acceptance limits.\n33\tPopenRunner reads at most cap + 1 byte; joining buffers temporarily duplicates\n34\tthat bounded storage (plus Python overhead), so this is not a cap on process RSS; an\n35\tinjected runner's own buffering is its responsibility. Nothing runs at import\n36\tor construction; there is no command-line entry point.\n37\t\"\"\"\n38\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n39\t\n40\tfrom collections.abc import Mapping\n41\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n42\timport json\n43\timport os\n44\timport re\n45\timport select\n46\timport subprocess\n47\timport time\n48\t\n49\tfrom first_transition_adapter import ROLES, digest\n50\tfrom first_transition_host_transport import SUPPORT_ROLES, _ids, host_command\n51\tfrom initial_transition_ops import Refused, require\n52\t\n53\tSCHEMA = 'igreja12.first-transition-host-manifest/1'\n54\tMANIFEST_KEYS = frozenset({'schema', 'daemon_id', 'legacy_project', 'network_id', 'service_ids', 'support_ids',\n55\t                           'processing_keys', 'gate_names'})\n56\tENTRIES = ('external', 'evolution-backend')\n57\tQUEUE_KEYS = ('pastorai:webhooks', 'pastorai:webhooks:processing', 'pastorai:webhooks:dead',\n58\t              'pastorai:webhooks:retry-scheduled')\n59\tREDIS_COMMANDS = ('TYPE', 'PTTL', 'LLEN', 'ZCARD')\n60\tREDIS_TYPES = ('none', 'string', 'list', 'set', 'zset', 'hash', 'stream')"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7c0715d-1aa9-47c4-a1be-b9d449b8e96c","uuid":"f8891345-5493-4839-bd29-23f3cdc6d65f","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:29:43.552Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_host_driver.py","content":"\"\"\"Observation/containment/resume driver behind ObservedHostTransport.\n\n``ObservedHostDriver.request(argv, *, timeout)`` answers the transport's\nsemantic commands from an injected runner plus explicit callbacks:\n\n* inspect-host: pinned daemon, pinned network and the seven pinned containers\n  through restricted ``--format`` stdout projections to Python, plus both ingress entries and the\n  unknown-writer callback;\n* redis-meta: TYPE/PTTL/LLEN/ZCARD on explicit keys via ``redis-cli`` inside the\n  pinned, label-verified Redis container; no KEYS/SCAN/values/auth in argv, and\n  an auth error is a refusal;\n* block-ingress, ``docker update --restart=no``, ``docker kill --signal=TERM``\n  and ``docker wait`` on the four legacy IDs only;\n* resume (``docker start``, ``docker update --restart=always`` on the four\n  legacy IDs and open-ingress through both bound entries) ONLY when a\n  ``ledger_proof`` bound to this manifest is injected: a fresh read-only\n  PostgreSQL proof (identity, exact baseline ledger, catalog; see\n  first_transition_database.LedgerProof) runs inside every resume request,\n  immediately before its effect. Without it, resume refuses before any call.\n\nEvery other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are\ncallback-reported scope-bound answers, not independent proof, and no token or\nboolean stands for a human approval. Docker values are CLI-reported for an\noperator-configured endpoint; nothing here certifies the host or quiescence.\nReal bindings/manifest values are Phase 3 inputs.\n\nThe Docker CLI applies --format client-side; only its restricted stdout\nprojection enters Python/journals. Tests use synthetic data only.\n\nErrors carry fixed codes only; runner output never enters exceptions, logs or\nreceipts. No retry: a timeout or refusal is final for that request. Each\nrequest has a cooperative deadline, checked after injected calls return; per-command output caps are acceptance limits.\nPopenRunner reads at most cap + 1 byte; joining buffers temporarily duplicates\nthat bounded storage (plus Python overhead), so this is not a cap on process RSS; an\ninjected runner's own buffering is its responsibility. Nothing runs at import\nor construction; there is no command-line entry point.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections.abc import Mapping\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport select\nimport subprocess\nimport time\n\nfrom first_transition_adapter import ROLES, digest\nfrom first_transition_host_transport import SUPPORT_ROLES, _ids, host_command\nfrom initial_transition_ops import Refused, require\n\nSCHEMA = 'igreja12.first-transition-host-manifest/1'\nMANIFEST_KEYS = frozenset({'schema', 'daemon_id', 'legacy_project', 'network_id', 'service_ids', 'support_ids',\n                           'processing_keys', 'gate_names'})\nENTRIES = ('external', 'evolution-backend')\nQUEUE_KEYS = ('pastorai:webhooks', 'pastorai:webhooks:processing', 'pastorai:webhooks:dead',\n              'pastorai:webhooks:retry-scheduled')\nREDIS_COMMANDS = ('TYPE', 'PTTL', 'LLEN', 'ZCARD')\nREDIS_TYPES = ('none', 'string', 'list', 'set', 'zset', 'hash', 'stream')","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":608}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MZAR4uLxQr9gGdRYQMSvAK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYfEWWGjV1hYVSW11Kjz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0122XhFdKmrApZaCasxRcc1U","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_host_driver.py","offset":185,"limit":80},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":47215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7c0715d-1aa9-47c4-a1be-b9d449b8e96c","uuid":"3527e010-aba0-4af2-8dff-f8f5be71ba0f","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:29:44.576Z","request_id":"req_011CgYfEW7DBRZ1jpDbo32JW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0122XhFdKmrApZaCasxRcc1U":{"file_path":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_host_driver.py","offset":185,"limit":80}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0122XhFdKmrApZaCasxRcc1U","type":"tool_result","content":"185\t\n186\tdef _tail(value, code):\n187\t    require(isinstance(value, list) and value and value[-1] is None, code)\n188\t    return value[:-1]\n189\t\n190\t\n191\tclass ObservedHostDriver:\n192\t    mode = 'observed-host'\n193\t\n194\t    def __init__(self, manifest, *, runner, ingress, writers, ledger_proof=None):\n195\t        require(isinstance(manifest, HostManifest), 'driver-manifest')\n196\t        manifest = manifest.validated()\n197\t        require(callable(runner), 'driver-runner')\n198\t        require(isinstance(ingress, Mapping) and set(ingress) == set(ENTRIES)\n199\t                and ingress['external'] is not ingress['evolution-backend']\n200\t                and all(self._bound(ingress[e], manifest, e, 'observe', 'block') for e in ENTRIES),\n201\t                'driver-ingress-binding')\n202\t        require(self._bound(writers, manifest, None, 'observe'), 'driver-writer-binding')\n203\t        require(ledger_proof is None or self._bound(ledger_proof, manifest, None, 'prove'), 'driver-ledger-binding')\n204\t        self.manifest, self.runner = manifest, runner\n205\t        self.ingress, self.writers, self.ledger_proof = dict(ingress), writers, ledger_proof\n206\t        self.template = inspect_template(manifest.gate_names)\n207\t        self.roles = {ident: role for role, ident in (*manifest.service_ids, *manifest.support_ids)}\n208\t        self.legacy = tuple(ident for _, ident in manifest.service_ids)\n209\t        self.redis_id = dict(manifest.support_ids)['redis']\n210\t        self.redis_verified = False\n211\t        self.refusals = []  # fixed codes only, for diagnosis; never output\n212\t        self._bindings_fixed = (self.ingress['external'], self.ingress['evolution-backend'], self.writers,\n213\t                                ledger_proof)\n214\t\n215\t    @property\n216\t    def supports_resume(self):\n217\t        # Resume needs the database proof and an opener on both ingress entries.\n218\t        return (self.ledger_proof is not None and self._bound(self.ledger_proof, self.manifest, None, 'prove')\n219\t                and all(self._bound(self.ingress[e], self.manifest, e, 'open') for e in ENTRIES))\n220\t\n221\t    @staticmethod\n222\t    def _bound(binding, manifest, entry, *methods):\n223\t        return (binding is not None and getattr(binding, 'scope', None) == manifest.digest\n224\t                and (entry is None or getattr(binding, 'entry', None) == entry)\n225\t                and all(callable(getattr(binding, method, None)) for method in methods))\n226\t\n227\t    def transport_scope(self):\n228\t        return self.manifest.transport_scope()\n229\t\n230\t    def request(self, argv, *, timeout):\n231\t        try:\n232\t            self._assert_bindings()\n233\t            result = self._dispatch(argv, timeout)\n234\t            self._assert_bindings()\n235\t            return result\n236\t        except Refused as exc:\n237\t            self.refusals = [*self.refusals[-63:], str(exc)]\n238\t            raise\n239\t\n240\t    def _assert_bindings(self):\n241\t        require(isinstance(self.ingress, dict) and set(self.ingress) == set(ENTRIES), 'driver-ingress-binding')\n242\t        for index, entry in enumerate(ENTRIES):\n243\t            require(self.ingress[entry] is self._bindings_fixed[index]\n244\t                    and self._bound(self.ingress[entry], self.manifest, entry, 'observe', 'block'),\n245\t                    'driver-ingress-binding')\n246\t        require(self.writers is self._bindings_fixed[2]\n247\t                and self._bound(self.writers, self.manifest, None, 'observe'), 'driver-writer-binding')\n248\t        require(self.ledger_proof is self._bindings_fixed[3], 'driver-ledger-binding')\n249\t\n250\t    def _dispatch(self, argv, timeout):\n251\t        require(type(timeout) in (int, float) and 0 < timeout <= 30, 'driver-timeout-bound')\n252\t        require(type(argv) is tuple and argv and all(type(a) is str for a in argv), 'driver-operation-forbidden')\n253\t        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout\n254\t        if argv == ('inspect-host',):\n255\t            return self._inspect_host(deadline)\n256\t        if argv[0] == 'redis-meta':\n257\t            require(len(argv) == 3 and argv[1] in REDIS_COMMANDS\n258\t                    and argv[2] in QUEUE_KEYS + self.manifest.processing_keys, 'driver-redis-scope')\n259\t            return self._redis_meta(argv[1], argv[2], deadline)\n260\t        if argv == ('block-ingress',):\n261\t            return self._block_ingress(deadline)\n262\t        if argv == ('open-ingress',):\n263\t            require(self.supports_resume, 'driver-operation-forbidden')\n264\t            return self._open_ingress(deadline)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7c0715d-1aa9-47c4-a1be-b9d449b8e96c","uuid":"2f7a80fb-158b-43cc-be91-b116911f69be","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:29:44.592Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_host_driver.py","content":"\ndef _tail(value, code):\n    require(isinstance(value, list) and value and value[-1] is None, code)\n    return value[:-1]\n\n\nclass ObservedHostDriver:\n    mode = 'observed-host'\n\n    def __init__(self, manifest, *, runner, ingress, writers, ledger_proof=None):\n        require(isinstance(manifest, HostManifest), 'driver-manifest')\n        manifest = manifest.validated()\n        require(callable(runner), 'driver-runner')\n        require(isinstance(ingress, Mapping) and set(ingress) == set(ENTRIES)\n                and ingress['external'] is not ingress['evolution-backend']\n                and all(self._bound(ingress[e], manifest, e, 'observe', 'block') for e in ENTRIES),\n                'driver-ingress-binding')\n        require(self._bound(writers, manifest, None, 'observe'), 'driver-writer-binding')\n        require(ledger_proof is None or self._bound(ledger_proof, manifest, None, 'prove'), 'driver-ledger-binding')\n        self.manifest, self.runner = manifest, runner\n        self.ingress, self.writers, self.ledger_proof = dict(ingress), writers, ledger_proof\n        self.template = inspect_template(manifest.gate_names)\n        self.roles = {ident: role for role, ident in (*manifest.service_ids, *manifest.support_ids)}\n        self.legacy = tuple(ident for _, ident in manifest.service_ids)\n        self.redis_id = dict(manifest.support_ids)['redis']\n        self.redis_verified = False\n        self.refusals = []  # fixed codes only, for diagnosis; never output\n        self._bindings_fixed = (self.ingress['external'], self.ingress['evolution-backend'], self.writers,\n                                ledger_proof)\n\n    @property\n    def supports_resume(self):\n        # Resume needs the database proof and an opener on both ingress entries.\n        return (self.ledger_proof is not None and self._bound(self.ledger_proof, self.manifest, None, 'prove')\n                and all(self._bound(self.ingress[e], self.manifest, e, 'open') for e in ENTRIES))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _bound(binding, manifest, entry, *methods):\n        return (binding is not None and getattr(binding, 'scope', None) == manifest.digest\n                and (entry is None or getattr(binding, 'entry', None) == entry)\n                and all(callable(getattr(binding, method, None)) for method in methods))\n\n    def transport_scope(self):\n        return self.manifest.transport_scope()\n\n    def request(self, argv, *, timeout):\n        try:\n            self._assert_bindings()\n            result = self._dispatch(argv, timeout)\n            self._assert_bindings()\n            return result\n        except Refused as exc:\n            self.refusals = [*self.refusals[-63:], str(exc)]\n            raise\n\n    def _assert_bindings(self):\n        require(isinstance(self.ingress, dict) and set(self.ingress) == set(ENTRIES), 'driver-ingress-binding')\n        for index, entry in enumerate(ENTRIES):\n            require(self.ingress[entry] is self._bindings_fixed[index]\n                    and self._bound(self.ingress[entry], self.manifest, entry, 'observe', 'block'),\n                    'driver-ingress-binding')\n        require(self.writers is self._bindings_fixed[2]\n                and self._bound(self.writers, self.manifest, None, 'observe'), 'driver-writer-binding')\n        require(self.ledger_proof is self._bindings_fixed[3], 'driver-ledger-binding')\n\n    def _dispatch(self, argv, timeout):\n        require(type(timeout) in (int, float) and 0 < timeout <= 30, 'driver-timeout-bound')\n        require(type(argv) is tuple and argv and all(type(a) is str for a in argv), 'driver-operation-forbidden')\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout\n        if argv == ('inspect-host',):\n            return self._inspect_host(deadline)\n        if argv[0] == 'redis-meta':\n            require(len(argv) == 3 and argv[1] in REDIS_COMMANDS\n                    and argv[2] in QUEUE_KEYS + self.manifest.processing_keys, 'driver-redis-scope')\n            return self._redis_meta(argv[1], argv[2], deadline)\n        if argv == ('block-ingress',):\n            return self._block_ingress(deadline)\n        if argv == ('open-ingress',):\n            require(self.supports_resume, 'driver-operation-forbidden')\n            return self._open_ingress(deadline)","numLines":80,"startLine":185,"totalLines":608}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0122XhFdKmrApZaCasxRcc1U","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
