{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYfN5VbbGBME5RNpeBNf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HSoB242GMmPpLhkBuw3fMT","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_orchestrator.py","old_string":"    Providers (database connection, secret, ingress/writer bindings, backup\n    receipt) are Phase 3 inputs; nothing is contacted while assembling.\n    \"\"\"","new_string":"    Providers (database connection, secret, ingress/writer bindings, backup\n    receipt) are Phase 3 inputs; nothing is contacted while assembling.\n\n    ``writers.observe()`` returns the number of UNKNOWN writers: sources outside\n    the declared allowed ones. Declared sources are this tool's own observer and\n    migration child and, from the A9 backend start on, the candidate backend of\n    ``config.candidate`` (its project/container name); none of them is an unknown\n    writer. Any other source (legacy service, consumer, foreign client) counts and\n    refuses. A binding that counted the candidate backend would fail closed at A9.\n    \"\"\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1924,"cache_read_input_tokens":92323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1924},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7c0715d-1aa9-47c4-a1be-b9d449b8e96c","uuid":"eb23d659-63ac-4106-873d-6c514741ee80","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:31:31.489Z","request_id":"req_011CgYfN53ZXsniojU1dmf7b","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HSoB242GMmPpLhkBuw3fMT":{"file_path":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_orchestrator.py","old_string":"    Providers (database connection, secret, ingress/writer bindings, backup\n    receipt) are Phase 3 inputs; nothing is contacted while assembling.\n    \"\"\"","new_string":"    Providers (database connection, secret, ingress/writer bindings, backup\n    receipt) are Phase 3 inputs; nothing is contacted while assembling.\n\n    ``writers.observe()`` returns the number of UNKNOWN writers: sources outside\n    the declared allowed ones. Declared sources are this tool's own observer and\n    migration child and, from the A9 backend start on, the candidate backend of\n    ``config.candidate`` (its project/container name); none of them is an unknown\n    writer. Any other source (legacy service, consumer, foreign client) counts and\n    refuses. A binding that counted the candidate backend would fail closed at A9.\n    \"\"\""}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HSoB242GMmPpLhkBuw3fMT","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_orchestrator.py has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7c0715d-1aa9-47c4-a1be-b9d449b8e96c","uuid":"cdc15ec8-618e-4f20-bb26-bdeb9e90040c","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:31:31.503Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_orchestrator.py","oldString":"    Providers (database connection, secret, ingress/writer bindings, backup\n    receipt) are Phase 3 inputs; nothing is contacted while assembling.\n    \"\"\"","newString":"    Providers (database connection, secret, ingress/writer bindings, backup\n    receipt) are Phase 3 inputs; nothing is contacted while assembling.\n\n    ``writers.observe()`` returns the number of UNKNOWN writers: sources outside\n    the declared allowed ones. Declared sources are this tool's own observer and\n    migration child and, from the A9 backend start on, the candidate backend of\n    ``config.candidate`` (its project/container name); none of them is an unknown\n    writer. Any other source (legacy service, consumer, foreign client) counts and\n    refuses. A binding that counted the candidate backend would fail closed at A9.\n    \"\"\"","originalFile":"\"\"\"First-transition orchestration over injected ports, up to A9 (never A10).\n\nSequence (one durable journal, shared with ObservedHostContract):\n\n1. fresh read-only database baseline equal to the configured expectation;\n2. ObservedHostContract.contain(): ingress blocked, four legacy restart=no,\n   SIGTERM, clean exit 0;\n3. two consecutive bounded fresh observations, each with the host still\n   contained and zero writing sessions and zero active leases in the database;\n4. injected backup/restore + clone rehearsal receipt validated against the plan,\n   identity and baseline (first_transition_adapter.validate_clone_receipt);\n5. final pre-DDL re-check, then the durable irrevocable ``ddl-marker``;\n6. the 51 pending migrations (43 transactional, 8 CONCURRENTLY) one by one via\n   the exact pinned ``backend/scripts/migrate.py`` bytes of the Plan, each with\n   a durable intent first; the first failure or doubt stops for good;\n7. candidate release layout ``<release_root>/<sha>`` (first_transition_candidate);\n8. A9: four candidate containers created held (restart=no, gates closed), ONLY\n   the backend started and smoked; consumers proven never started; legacy\n   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout.\n\nRecovery is objective (``recovery()``), never automatic: no undo, no retry of a\ndestructive operation, no legacy resume once the DDL marker exists. A\npre-DDL legacy resume goes through ObservedHostContract.resume_legacy, whose\ndriver requires a fresh read-only ledger proof before every effect.\n\nConfiguration (``load_config``) holds public values only; secrets reach the\nmigration child exclusively through its isolated environment. Nothing runs at\nimport; there is no command-line entry point and no production operation here.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport subprocess\nimport time\n\nfrom first_transition_adapter import APPLICATION_SHA, EXECUTOR_SHA, ROLES, Plan, digest, validate_clone_receipt\nfrom first_transition_candidate import (CONSUMERS, CandidatePort, CandidateRunner, CandidateSpec, check_backend_running,\n                                        check_held, check_identity, write_candidate_release, write_hold_override)\nfrom first_transition_database import (LEASES, DatabaseExpectation, LedgerProof, ReadOnlyDatabase, require_ddl_free,\n                                       require_quiet, require_same_database, summary)\nfrom first_transition_host_contract import ObservedHostContract\nfrom first_transition_host_driver import HostManifest, ObservedHostDriver, PopenRunner, _absolute\nfrom first_transition_host_transport import ObservedHostTransport\nfrom initial_transition_files import Journal, no_symlink, read_regular\nfrom initial_transition_ops import Refused, require\n\nCONFIG_SCHEMA = 'igreja12.first-transition-config/1'\nCONFIG_KEYS = frozenset({'schema', 'repo', 'state_dir', 'migration_workdir', 'python', 'docker', 'database',\n                         'host', 'candidate', 'package_manifest_sha256', 'timeouts'})\nTIMEOUTS = dict(migration_s=300, observe_s=10, quiescence_interval_s=5, quiescence_budget_s=60)\nSHAPE = (51, 43, 8)  # pending, transactional, CONCURRENTLY\nPROCEDURES = {\n    'not-started': 'nothing intended: no recovery action',\n    'containment-partial': 'replay run(): contain() never re-signals; an unclean exit stays refused for a human',\n    'contained-pre-ddl': 'replay run() or resume_legacy(token): fresh ledger proof before every effect',\n    'resume-partial': 'replay resume_legacy(token): receipted roles re-proven, ledger proof per effect',\n    'legacy-resumed': 'legacy back with ingress open: start a new journal for any later attempt',\n    'ddl-ambiguous': 'stop: no retry, no legacy; inspect ledger/indexes read-only and decide restore (A6) or completion',\n    'ddl-failed': 'stop: no retry, no legacy; restore from the validated backup (A6) or fix forward by a new decision',\n    'post-ddl-failed': 'stop: no legacy; keep ingress blocked and inspect the failure read-only before a decision',\n    'candidate-ambiguous': 'stop: no undo; inspect the candidate project read-only, nothing restarted or removed',\n    'candidate-failed': 'stop: no undo; consumers stay held, ingress blocked; human decision on the backend',\n    'a9-complete': 'hold: backend smoked, consumers held, ingress blocked; A10 needs its own authorization',\n}\nPROCESS_ENV = frozenset({'PATH', 'LC_ALL', 'LANG', 'PYTHON_DOTENV_DISABLED', 'MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL', 'PGAPPNAME',\n                         'PGCONNECT_TIMEOUT'})\n\n\nclass ProcessRunner:\n    \"\"\"Generic safe runner: allowlisted absolute binaries, constructed env, no shell, output discarded.\n\n    The environment is the only channel for secrets: argv never carries one and\n    no output is captured, so nothing can reach logs or exceptions.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, *, binaries, run=None):\n        require(isinstance(binaries, tuple) and binaries and all(_absolute(b) for b in binaries)\n                and (run is None or callable(run)), 'process-runner-config')\n        self.binaries, self.run = binaries, run\n\n    def __call__(self, argv, *, env, cwd, timeout):\n        require(type(argv) is tuple and argv and argv[0] in self.binaries\n                and all(type(a) is str and 0 < len(a) <= 4096 and '\\x00' not in a for a in argv), 'process-argv')\n        require(isinstance(env, dict) and set(env) <= PROCESS_ENV\n                and all(type(v) is str and '\\x00' not in v for v in env.values()), 'process-env')\n        require(_absolute(cwd) and type(timeout) in (int, float) and 0 < timeout <= 3600, 'process-bounds')\n        run = self.run or subprocess.run  # resolved per call, never at import/construction\n        outcome = None\n        try:\n            done = run(list(argv), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n                       env=dict(env), cwd=cwd, timeout=timeout, close_fds=True, shell=False, check=False)\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n            outcome = 'timeout'\n        except Exception:\n            outcome = 'process-spawn-failed'\n        if outcome == 'timeout':\n            raise TimeoutError('process-timeout')\n        require(outcome is None and type(getattr(done, 'returncode', None)) is int, outcome or 'process-failed')\n        return done.returncode\n\n\nclass MigrationExecutor:\n    \"\"\"One pending migration through the exact pinned migrate.py bytes of the Plan.\n\n    ``python <dir>/scripts/migrate.py apply <name> --yes [--no-transaction]``\n    in a fresh exclusive directory under the configured workdir; the database\n    URL comes from ``secret()`` straight into the child environment.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, plan, *, python, workdir, secret, runner, timeout=300):\n        require(isinstance(plan, Plan) and plan.application_sha == APPLICATION_SHA\n                and plan.executor_sha == EXECUTOR_SHA, 'migration-plan')\n        require(_absolute(python) and _absolute(workdir) and callable(secret) and callable(runner)\n                and type(timeout) is int and 0 < timeout <= 3600, 'migration-executor-config')\n        self.plan, self.python, self.workdir = plan, python, workdir\n        self.secret, self.runner, self.timeout = secret, runner, timeout\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def command(python, directory, migration):\n        return (python, '-I', f'{directory}/scripts/migrate.py', 'apply', migration.name, '--yes',\n                *(('--no-transaction',) if migration.concurrent else ()))\n\n    def _materialize(self, index, migration):\n        root = no_symlink(Path(self.workdir))\n        require(os.path.lexists(root) and stat.S_ISDIR(os.lstat(root).st_mode), 'migration-workdir-missing')\n        directory = root / f'{index:02d}-{self.plan.digest[:16]}'\n        try:\n            directory.mkdir(mode=0o700)  # exclusive: a previous attempt's directory refuses\n        except FileExistsError:\n            raise Refused('migration-workdir-exists') from None\n        (directory / 'scripts').mkdir(mode=0o700)\n        (directory / 'migrations').mkdir(mode=0o700)\n        for path, data in (('scripts/migrate.py', self.plan.executor), ('migrations/' + migration.name, migration.sql)):\n            fd = os.open(directory / path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)\n            with os.fdopen(fd, 'wb') as handle:\n                handle.write(data)\n        return str(directory)\n\n    def apply(self, index, migration):\n        require(migration in self.plan.pending and self.plan.pending[index - 1] is migration, 'migration-not-pending')\n        directory = self._materialize(index, migration)\n        url = self.secret()\n        require(isinstance(url, str) and url.startswith('postgresql://') and '\\n' not in url, 'migration-secret')\n        env = dict(PATH='/usr/bin:/bin', LC_ALL='C', PYTHON_DOTENV_DISABLED='1', MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=url,\n                   PGAPPNAME=f'pastorai-first-transition-{index:02d}', PGCONNECT_TIMEOUT='10')\n        return self.runner(self.command(self.python, directory, migration), env=env, cwd=directory,\n                           timeout=self.timeout)\n\n\nclass FirstTransition:\n    def __init__(self, *, plan, journal, host, database, expected, backup_proof, executor, layout, candidate,\n                 config_digest, clock=time.monotonic, sleep=time.sleep, timeouts=None):\n        for value, kind, code in ((plan, Plan, 'plan'), (journal, Journal, 'journal'),\n                                  (host, ObservedHostContract, 'host'), (database, ReadOnlyDatabase, 'database'),\n                                  (expected, DatabaseExpectation, 'expectation'),\n                                  (executor, MigrationExecutor, 'executor'), (candidate, CandidatePort, 'candidate')):\n            require(isinstance(value, kind), 'transition-' + code + '-missing')\n        require(callable(backup_proof), 'transition-backup-missing')\n        require(callable(layout), 'transition-layout-missing')\n        require(journal.lock_fd is not None and host.j is journal, 'transition-journal')\n        require(executor.plan is plan and candidate.spec.sha == plan.application_sha, 'transition-plan-binding')\n        pending = plan.pending\n        require((len(pending), sum(not m.concurrent for m in pending), sum(m.concurrent for m in pending)) == SHAPE,\n                'transition-release-shape')\n        require(expected.validated().ledger == plan.baseline, 'transition-expectation-baseline')\n        require(isinstance(config_digest, str) and re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{64}', config_digest), 'transition-config')\n        self.t = {**TIMEOUTS, **(timeouts or {})}\n        self.plan, self.j, self.host, self.db, self.expected = plan, journal, host, database, expected\n        self.backup_proof, self.executor, self.layout, self.candidate = backup_proof, executor, layout, candidate\n        self.config_digest, self.clock, self.sleep = config_digest, clock, sleep\n\n    # -- journal helpers -------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def _intent(self, step, **fields):\n        return self.j.append('transition-intent', step=step, **fields)\n\n    def _done(self, step, **fields):\n        return self.j.append('transition-done', step=step, **fields)\n\n    def _open(self, step):\n        \"\"\"Intent without receipt: the outcome is unknown and never retried automatically.\"\"\"\n        return (self.j.last('transition-intent', step) is not None\n                and self.j.last('transition-done', step) is None)\n\n    def _observe(self):\n        return self.db.observe(timeout=self.t['observe_s'])\n\n    def _init(self):\n        init = self.j.last('transition-init')\n        values = dict(plan_digest=self.plan.digest, config_digest=self.config_digest,\n                      baseline_digest=self.expected.baseline_digest, application_sha=self.plan.application_sha,\n                      executor_sha=self.plan.executor_sha, candidate_image=self.candidate.spec.image)\n        if init is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-init', production_ready=False, **values)\n        else:\n            require(all(init.get(k) == v for k, v in values.items()), 'transition-inputs-changed')\n\n    # -- entry points --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def run(self):\n        self._init()\n        require(self.j.last('observed-host-intent', 'legacy-resume') is None, 'transition-legacy-resume-started')\n        require(self.j.last('transition-failed') is None, 'transition-stopped')  # first failure is final\n        try:\n            if self.j.last('ddl-marker') is None:\n                self._baseline()\n                self.host.contain()\n                self._quiesce()\n                self._backup()\n                self._mark_ddl()\n            self._migrate()\n            self._release_layout()\n            return self._a9()\n        except BaseException as exc:\n            if self.j.last('ddl-marker') is not None:\n                self.j.append('transition-failed', code=str(exc) if isinstance(exc, Refused) else 'interrupted',\n                              legacy_resume_allowed=False)\n            raise\n\n    def resume_legacy(self, confirmation, *, allow_queue_drift=False):\n        \"\"\"Pre-DDL only; the contract and the driver's ledger proof re-check everything.\"\"\"\n        require(self.j.last('ddl-marker') is None and not self.j.find('transition-intent'),\n                'post-ddl-resume-forbidden')\n        return self.host.resume_legacy(confirmation, allow_queue_drift=allow_queue_drift)\n\n    # -- pre-DDL ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def _baseline(self):\n        observation = self._observe()\n        require_ddl_free(observation, self.expected)\n        if self.j.last('transition-baseline') is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-baseline', evidence='database-read-only', **summary(observation))\n\n    def _quiet_observation(self):\n        receipt = self.host.assert_contained()\n        observation = self._observe()\n        require_ddl_free(observation, self.expected)\n        require_quiet(observation)\n        return receipt['fingerprint'], receipt['queue_digest'], summary(observation)\n\n    def _quiesce(self):\n        start = self.clock()\n        first = self._quiet_observation()\n        self.sleep(self.t['quiescence_interval_s'])\n        second = self._quiet_observation()\n        require(self.clock() - start <= self.t['quiescence_budget_s'], 'transition-quiescence-unbounded')\n        require(first == second, 'transition-quiescence-changed')\n        self.j.append('transition-quiescent', observations=2, writing_sessions=0, active_leases=0,\n                      host_fingerprint=first[0], queue_digest=first[1], evidence='database-read-only')\n\n    def _backup(self):\n        receipt = self.backup_proof()\n        require(isinstance(receipt, dict), 'clone-receipt-invalid')\n        validate_clone_receipt(receipt, self.plan, self.expected.identity, self.expected.baseline_digest)\n        recorded = self.j.last('transition-backup')\n        if recorded is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-backup', receipt_digest=digest(receipt), restore_verified=True)\n        else:\n            require(recorded['receipt_digest'] == digest(receipt), 'transition-backup-changed')\n        return digest(receipt)\n\n    def _mark_ddl(self):\n        require(self.j.last('transition-quiescent') is not None, 'transition-not-quiescent')\n        # Immediately before the irrevocable marker: contained, read-only baseline, quiet, backup valid.\n        self._quiet_observation()\n        backup = self._backup()\n        self.j.append('ddl-marker', irrevocable=True, pending=[m.name for m in self.plan.pending],\n                      baseline_digest=self.expected.baseline_digest, backup_digest=backup,\n                      legacy_resume_allowed=False)\n\n    # -- DDL ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def _migrate(self):\n        ledger = list(self.plan.baseline)\n        for index, migration in enumerate(self.plan.pending, 1):\n            step = 'migration:' + migration.name\n            if self.j.last('transition-done', step) is not None:\n                ledger.append(migration.name)\n                continue\n            require(self.j.last('transition-intent', step) is None, 'migration-outcome-ambiguous')\n            before = self._observe()\n            require_same_database(before, self.expected)\n            require(list(before['ledger']) == sorted(ledger), 'migration-ledger-not-prefix')\n            require(not before['invalid'] and before['index_builds'] == 0, 'database-ddl-in-progress')\n            require_quiet(before)\n            self.host.assert_contained()\n            self._intent(step, index=index, sql_sha256=migration.sha256, concurrent=migration.concurrent)\n            try:\n                code = self.executor.apply(index, migration)\n            except TimeoutError:\n                code = None\n            after = self._observe()\n            failure = self._migration_failure(migration, code, ledger, after, self.expected)\n            if failure is not None:\n                # Definite only for a transactional rollback with no trace; anything else is ambiguous.\n                definite = (failure == 'migration-failed' and not migration.concurrent\n                            and not after['invalid'] and after['index_builds'] == 0)\n                self.j.append('transition-migration-failed', step=step, code=failure, definite=definite)\n                raise Refused(failure)\n            self._done(step, ledger_digest=after['ledger_digest'])\n            ledger.append(migration.name)\n        final = self._observe()\n        require_same_database(final, self.expected)  # before transition-migrated, layout and A9\n        require(list(final['ledger']) == sorted(m.name for m in self.plan.migrations), 'final-ledger')\n        if self.j.last('transition-migrated') is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-migrated', ledger=len(final['ledger']), catalog=final['catalog'])\n        else:\n            require(self.j.last('transition-migrated')['catalog'] == final['catalog'], 'database-ddl-drift')\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _migration_failure(migration, code, ledger, after, expected):\n        # A ledger read from another (or not read-only/visible) database proves nothing: ambiguous.\n        try:\n            require_same_database(after, expected)\n        except Refused as exc:\n            return str(exc)\n        applied = list(after['ledger']) == sorted([*ledger, migration.name])\n        if code is None:\n            return 'migration-timeout'\n        if code != 0:\n            return 'migration-ambiguous-ledger-without-success' if applied else 'migration-failed'\n        if not applied:\n            return 'migration-ambiguous-exit0-no-ledger'\n        if after['invalid'] or after['index_builds'] or not set(migration.indexes) <= set(after['indexes']):\n            return 'migration-index-invalid'\n        return None\n\n    def _release_layout(self):\n        if self.j.last('transition-done', 'layout') is None:\n            self._intent('layout')\n        files = self.layout()  # exclusive or byte-for-byte verification, on every invocation\n        if self.j.last('transition-done', 'layout') is None:\n            self._done('layout', files=files)\n\n    # -- A9 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def _candidate_states(self, ids):\n        states = self.candidate.inspect(tuple(ids[r] for r in ROLES))\n        result = {role: states[ids[role]] for role in ROLES}\n        for role, state in result.items():\n            check_identity(self.candidate.spec, role, state)\n        return result\n\n    def _held(self, ids, created, backend_started):\n        \"\"\"Consumers never started, legacy contained, support preserved, ingress blocked.\"\"\"\n        states = self._candidate_states(ids)\n        for role in CONSUMERS:\n            check_held(states[role], created[role])\n        if backend_started is None:\n            check_held(states['backend'], created['backend'])\n        else:\n            check_backend_running(states['backend'], backend_started)\n        self.host.assert_contained()\n        return states\n\n    def _a9(self):\n        created = self.j.last('transition-done', 'a9:create')\n        if created is None:\n            require(not self._open('a9:create'), 'candidate-create-ambiguous')\n            self.host.assert_contained()\n            require(self.candidate.project_ids() == (), 'candidate-project-not-empty')\n            write_hold_override(self.candidate.spec)\n            self._intent('a9:create', project=self.candidate.spec.project)\n            self.candidate.create_held()\n            found = self.candidate.project_ids()\n            require(len(found) == 4, 'candidate-create-scope')\n            states = self.candidate.inspect(found)\n            ids = {state['service']: ident for ident, state in states.items()}\n            require(set(ids) == set(ROLES), 'candidate-create-scope')\n            for role in ROLES:\n                check_identity(self.candidate.spec, role, states[ids[role]])\n                check_held(states[ids[role]])\n            created = self._done('a9:create', ids=ids, created={\n                role: dict(started=states[ids[role]]['started'], restart_count=states[ids[role]]['restart_count'])\n                for role in ROLES})\n        ids, snapshot = created['ids'], created['created']\n        require(self.candidate.project_ids() == tuple(sorted(ids.values())), 'candidate-project-changed')\n        started = self.j.last('transition-done', 'a9:start-backend')\n        if started is None:\n            require(not self._open('a9:start-backend'), 'candidate-start-ambiguous')\n            self._held(ids, snapshot, None)\n            self._intent('a9:start-backend', id=ids['backend'])\n            self.candidate.start_backend(ids['backend'])\n            state = self._candidate_states(ids)['backend']\n            check_backend_running(state)\n            started = self._done('a9:start-backend', started=state['started'])\n        self._held(ids, snapshot, started['started'])\n        smoke = self.candidate.smoke(ids['backend'])  # fresh read-only probe on every invocation\n        self._held(ids, snapshot, started['started'])\n        if self.j.last('transition-a9-complete') is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-a9-complete', smoke=smoke, consumers='held', ingress_blocked=True,\n                          a10='not-implemented')\n        return dict(status='a9-backend-smoked', smoke=smoke, consumers='held', ingress_blocked=True,\n                    legacy_resume_allowed=False, a10='not-implemented', production_ready=False)\n\n    # -- recovery --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def recovery(self):\n        \"\"\"Objective classification of the journal; never performs an action.\"\"\"\n        j = self.j\n        open_steps = [e['step'] for e in j.find('transition-intent') if self._open(e['step'])]\n        failed = j.last('transition-failed')\n        if j.last('transition-a9-complete') is not None and failed is None:\n            state = 'a9-complete'\n        elif j.last('ddl-marker') is not None:\n            migrations = [s for s in open_steps if s.startswith('migration:')]\n            if migrations:\n                outcome = j.last('transition-migration-failed', migrations[-1])\n                state = 'ddl-failed' if outcome is not None and outcome['definite'] is True else 'ddl-ambiguous'\n            elif any(s.startswith('a9:') for s in open_steps):\n                state = 'candidate-ambiguous'\n            elif j.last('transition-done', 'layout') is not None and failed is not None:\n                state = 'candidate-failed'\n            else:\n                state = 'post-ddl-failed'\n        elif j.last('observed-host-resumed') is not None:\n            state = 'legacy-resumed'\n        elif j.last('observed-host-intent', 'legacy-resume') is not None:\n            state = 'resume-partial'\n        elif j.last('observed-host-contained') is not None:\n            state = 'contained-pre-ddl'\n        elif j.find('observed-host-intent'):\n            state = 'containment-partial'\n        else:\n            state = 'not-started'\n        return dict(state=state, procedure=PROCEDURES[state], open_steps=open_steps,\n                    legacy_resume_allowed=state in ('contained-pre-ddl', 'resume-partial'),\n                    automatic_undo=False, destructive_retry=False)\n\n\n# -- configuration ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass FirstTransitionConfig:\n    repo: str\n    state_dir: str\n    migration_workdir: str\n    python: str\n    docker: tuple\n    catalog: str\n    identity: str\n    lease_columns: tuple\n    observer_applications: tuple\n    manifest: HostManifest\n    candidate: CandidateSpec\n    package_manifest_sha256: str\n    timeouts: tuple\n    digest: str\n\n\ndef parse_config(data):\n    \"\"\"Public values only: unknown keys (a password, a URL) refuse.\"\"\"\n    require(isinstance(data, dict) and set(data) == CONFIG_KEYS and data['schema'] == CONFIG_SCHEMA, 'config-keys')\n    docker, database, candidate, timeouts = data['docker'], data['database'], data['candidate'], data['timeouts']\n    require(isinstance(docker, dict) and set(docker) == {'binary', 'endpoint', 'config_dir'}, 'config-docker')\n    require(isinstance(database, dict) and set(database) == {\n        'identity', 'catalog', 'lease_columns', 'observer_applications'}, 'config-database')\n    require(isinstance(candidate, dict) and set(candidate) == {\n        'sha', 'image', 'project', 'containers', 'network_name', 'release_root', 'hold_override', 'env_file',\n        'smoke_seconds'}, 'config-candidate')\n    require(isinstance(timeouts, dict) and set(timeouts) <= set(TIMEOUTS)\n            and all(type(v) is int and 0 < v <= 3600 for v in timeouts.values())\n            and timeouts.get('observe_s', TIMEOUTS['observe_s']) <= 30, 'config-timeouts')\n    require(all(_absolute(data[k]) for k in ('repo', 'state_dir', 'migration_workdir', 'python')), 'config-paths')\n    require(isinstance(database['lease_columns'], list) and isinstance(database['observer_applications'], list)\n            and all(isinstance(p, list) for p in database['lease_columns']), 'config-database')\n    manifest = HostManifest.from_dict(data['host'])\n    containers = candidate['containers']\n    require(isinstance(containers, dict) and set(containers) == set(ROLES), 'config-candidate')\n    spec = CandidateSpec(sha=candidate['sha'], image=candidate['image'], project=candidate['project'],\n                         containers=tuple((r, containers[r]) for r in ROLES), network_id=manifest.network_id,\n                         network_name=candidate['network_name'], release_root=candidate['release_root'],\n                         hold_override=candidate['hold_override'], env_file=candidate['env_file'],\n                         daemon_id=manifest.daemon_id, smoke_seconds=candidate['smoke_seconds']).validated()\n    require(spec.sha == APPLICATION_SHA, 'config-candidate-sha')\n    require(isinstance(data['package_manifest_sha256'], str)\n            and re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{64}', data['package_manifest_sha256']), 'config-package')\n    canonical = json.dumps(data, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')).encode()\n    return FirstTransitionConfig(\n        repo=data['repo'], state_dir=data['state_dir'], migration_workdir=data['migration_workdir'],\n        python=data['python'], docker=(docker['binary'], docker['endpoint'], docker['config_dir']),\n        catalog=database['catalog'], identity=database['identity'],\n        lease_columns=tuple(tuple(p) for p in database['lease_columns']) or LEASES,\n        observer_applications=tuple(database['observer_applications']), manifest=manifest, candidate=spec,\n        package_manifest_sha256=data['package_manifest_sha256'], timeouts=tuple(sorted(timeouts.items())),\n        digest=hashlib.sha256(canonical).hexdigest())\n\n\ndef load_config(path):\n    try:\n        data = json.loads(read_regular(path, 64 * 1024))\n    except ValueError:\n        raise Refused('config-invalid-json') from None\n    return parse_config(data)\n\n\ndef assemble(config, *, plan, journal, connect, secret, ingress, writers, backup_proof, popen=None, run=None,\n             clock=time.monotonic, sleep=time.sleep, git=None):\n    \"\"\"Wire real ports from configuration plus injected providers; any absent provider refuses.\n\n    Providers (database connection, secret, ingress/writer bindings, backup\n    receipt) are Phase 3 inputs; nothing is contacted while assembling.\n    \"\"\"\n    require(isinstance(config, FirstTransitionConfig), 'transition-config')\n    for value, code in ((connect, 'database'), (secret, 'secret'), (backup_proof, 'backup')):\n        require(callable(value), 'transition-' + code + '-missing')\n    require(ingress is not None and writers is not None, 'transition-host-bindings-missing')\n    binary, endpoint, config_dir = config.docker\n    database = ReadOnlyDatabase(connect, lease_columns=config.lease_columns,\n                                observer_applications=config.observer_applications)\n    expected = DatabaseExpectation(config.identity, plan.baseline, config.catalog).validated()\n    proof = LedgerProof(database, expected, scope=config.manifest.digest)\n    driver = ObservedHostDriver(config.manifest, ingress=ingress, writers=writers, ledger_proof=proof,\n                                runner=PopenRunner(docker_binary=binary, endpoint=endpoint, config_dir=config_dir,\n                                                   popen=popen, resume=True))\n    host = ObservedHostContract(ObservedHostTransport(driver, **config.manifest.transport_scope()), journal)\n    candidate = CandidatePort(config.candidate, runner=CandidateRunner(\n        config.candidate, docker_binary=binary, endpoint=endpoint, config_dir=config_dir, popen=popen))\n    executor = MigrationExecutor(plan, python=config.python, workdir=config.migration_workdir, secret=secret,\n                                 runner=ProcessRunner(binaries=(config.python,), run=run),\n                                 timeout=dict(config.timeouts).get('migration_s', TIMEOUTS['migration_s']))\n    migrations = [m.name for m in plan.migrations]\n\n    def layout():\n        return write_candidate_release(config.repo, config.candidate, config.manifest, migrations=migrations,\n                                       package_manifest_sha256=config.package_manifest_sha256, git=git)\n    return FirstTransition(plan=plan, journal=journal, host=host, database=database, expected=expected,\n                           backup_proof=backup_proof, executor=executor, layout=layout, candidate=candidate,\n                           config_digest=config.digest, clock=clock, sleep=sleep, timeouts=dict(config.timeouts))\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":499,"oldLines":6,"newStart":499,"newLines":13,"lines":[" ","     Providers (database connection, secret, ingress/writer bindings, backup","     receipt) are Phase 3 inputs; nothing is contacted while assembling.","+","+    ``writers.observe()`` returns the number of UNKNOWN writers: sources outside","+    the declared allowed ones. Declared sources are this tool's own observer and","+    migration child and, from the A9 backend start on, the candidate backend of","+    ``config.candidate`` (its project/container name); none of them is an unknown","+    writer. Any other source (legacy service, consumer, foreign client) counts and","+    refuses. A binding that counted the candidate backend would fail closed at A9.","     \"\"\"","     require(isinstance(config, FirstTransitionConfig), 'transition-config')","     for value, code in ((connect, 'database'), (secret, 'secret'), (backup_proof, 'backup')):"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HSoB242GMmPpLhkBuw3fMT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYfN5VbbGBME5RNpeBNf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VSmTvhkcuoMqdasCu472Nh","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_orchestrator.py","old_string":"   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout.\n","new_string":"   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout. The running\n   candidate backend is a declared allowed source for the injected writer\n   binding (see ``assemble``), never an unknown writer.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1924,"cache_read_input_tokens":92323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1924},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7c0715d-1aa9-47c4-a1be-b9d449b8e96c","uuid":"a5804450-e853-4f64-9b3b-f214804227c5","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:31:33.252Z","request_id":"req_011CgYfN53ZXsniojU1dmf7b","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VSmTvhkcuoMqdasCu472Nh":{"file_path":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_orchestrator.py","old_string":"   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout.\n","new_string":"   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout. The running\n   candidate backend is a declared allowed source for the injected writer\n   binding (see ``assemble``), never an unknown writer.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VSmTvhkcuoMqdasCu472Nh","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_orchestrator.py has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7c0715d-1aa9-47c4-a1be-b9d449b8e96c","uuid":"996ca9ab-c8b9-49e8-9a5f-7db5c00b98e8","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:31:33.280Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_orchestrator.py","oldString":"   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout.\n","newString":"   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout. The running\n   candidate backend is a declared allowed source for the injected writer\n   binding (see ``assemble``), never an unknown writer.\n","originalFile":"\"\"\"First-transition orchestration over injected ports, up to A9 (never A10).\n\nSequence (one durable journal, shared with ObservedHostContract):\n\n1. fresh read-only database baseline equal to the configured expectation;\n2. ObservedHostContract.contain(): ingress blocked, four legacy restart=no,\n   SIGTERM, clean exit 0;\n3. two consecutive bounded fresh observations, each with the host still\n   contained and zero writing sessions and zero active leases in the database;\n4. injected backup/restore + clone rehearsal receipt validated against the plan,\n   identity and baseline (first_transition_adapter.validate_clone_receipt);\n5. final pre-DDL re-check, then the durable irrevocable ``ddl-marker``;\n6. the 51 pending migrations (43 transactional, 8 CONCURRENTLY) one by one via\n   the exact pinned ``backend/scripts/migrate.py`` bytes of the Plan, each with\n   a durable intent first; the first failure or doubt stops for good;\n7. candidate release layout ``<release_root>/<sha>`` (first_transition_candidate);\n8. A9: four candidate containers created held (restart=no, gates closed), ONLY\n   the backend started and smoked; consumers proven never started; legacy\n   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout.\n\nRecovery is objective (``recovery()``), never automatic: no undo, no retry of a\ndestructive operation, no legacy resume once the DDL marker exists. A\npre-DDL legacy resume goes through ObservedHostContract.resume_legacy, whose\ndriver requires a fresh read-only ledger proof before every effect.\n\nConfiguration (``load_config``) holds public values only; secrets reach the\nmigration child exclusively through its isolated environment. Nothing runs at\nimport; there is no command-line entry point and no production operation here.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport subprocess\nimport time\n\nfrom first_transition_adapter import APPLICATION_SHA, EXECUTOR_SHA, ROLES, Plan, digest, validate_clone_receipt\nfrom first_transition_candidate import (CONSUMERS, CandidatePort, CandidateRunner, CandidateSpec, check_backend_running,\n                                        check_held, check_identity, write_candidate_release, write_hold_override)\nfrom first_transition_database import (LEASES, DatabaseExpectation, LedgerProof, ReadOnlyDatabase, require_ddl_free,\n                                       require_quiet, require_same_database, summary)\nfrom first_transition_host_contract import ObservedHostContract\nfrom first_transition_host_driver import HostManifest, ObservedHostDriver, PopenRunner, _absolute\nfrom first_transition_host_transport import ObservedHostTransport\nfrom initial_transition_files import Journal, no_symlink, read_regular\nfrom initial_transition_ops import Refused, require\n\nCONFIG_SCHEMA = 'igreja12.first-transition-config/1'\nCONFIG_KEYS = frozenset({'schema', 'repo', 'state_dir', 'migration_workdir', 'python', 'docker', 'database',\n                         'host', 'candidate', 'package_manifest_sha256', 'timeouts'})\nTIMEOUTS = dict(migration_s=300, observe_s=10, quiescence_interval_s=5, quiescence_budget_s=60)\nSHAPE = (51, 43, 8)  # pending, transactional, CONCURRENTLY\nPROCEDURES = {\n    'not-started': 'nothing intended: no recovery action',\n    'containment-partial': 'replay run(): contain() never re-signals; an unclean exit stays refused for a human',\n    'contained-pre-ddl': 'replay run() or resume_legacy(token): fresh ledger proof before every effect',\n    'resume-partial': 'replay resume_legacy(token): receipted roles re-proven, ledger proof per effect',\n    'legacy-resumed': 'legacy back with ingress open: start a new journal for any later attempt',\n    'ddl-ambiguous': 'stop: no retry, no legacy; inspect ledger/indexes read-only and decide restore (A6) or completion',\n    'ddl-failed': 'stop: no retry, no legacy; restore from the validated backup (A6) or fix forward by a new decision',\n    'post-ddl-failed': 'stop: no legacy; keep ingress blocked and inspect the failure read-only before a decision',\n    'candidate-ambiguous': 'stop: no undo; inspect the candidate project read-only, nothing restarted or removed',\n    'candidate-failed': 'stop: no undo; consumers stay held, ingress blocked; human decision on the backend',\n    'a9-complete': 'hold: backend smoked, consumers held, ingress blocked; A10 needs its own authorization',\n}\nPROCESS_ENV = frozenset({'PATH', 'LC_ALL', 'LANG', 'PYTHON_DOTENV_DISABLED', 'MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL', 'PGAPPNAME',\n                         'PGCONNECT_TIMEOUT'})\n\n\nclass ProcessRunner:\n    \"\"\"Generic safe runner: allowlisted absolute binaries, constructed env, no shell, output discarded.\n\n    The environment is the only channel for secrets: argv never carries one and\n    no output is captured, so nothing can reach logs or exceptions.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, *, binaries, run=None):\n        require(isinstance(binaries, tuple) and binaries and all(_absolute(b) for b in binaries)\n                and (run is None or callable(run)), 'process-runner-config')\n        self.binaries, self.run = binaries, run\n\n    def __call__(self, argv, *, env, cwd, timeout):\n        require(type(argv) is tuple and argv and argv[0] in self.binaries\n                and all(type(a) is str and 0 < len(a) <= 4096 and '\\x00' not in a for a in argv), 'process-argv')\n        require(isinstance(env, dict) and set(env) <= PROCESS_ENV\n                and all(type(v) is str and '\\x00' not in v for v in env.values()), 'process-env')\n        require(_absolute(cwd) and type(timeout) in (int, float) and 0 < timeout <= 3600, 'process-bounds')\n        run = self.run or subprocess.run  # resolved per call, never at import/construction\n        outcome = None\n        try:\n            done = run(list(argv), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n                       env=dict(env), cwd=cwd, timeout=timeout, close_fds=True, shell=False, check=False)\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n            outcome = 'timeout'\n        except Exception:\n            outcome = 'process-spawn-failed'\n        if outcome == 'timeout':\n            raise TimeoutError('process-timeout')\n        require(outcome is None and type(getattr(done, 'returncode', None)) is int, outcome or 'process-failed')\n        return done.returncode\n\n\nclass MigrationExecutor:\n    \"\"\"One pending migration through the exact pinned migrate.py bytes of the Plan.\n\n    ``python <dir>/scripts/migrate.py apply <name> --yes [--no-transaction]``\n    in a fresh exclusive directory under the configured workdir; the database\n    URL comes from ``secret()`` straight into the child environment.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, plan, *, python, workdir, secret, runner, timeout=300):\n        require(isinstance(plan, Plan) and plan.application_sha == APPLICATION_SHA\n                and plan.executor_sha == EXECUTOR_SHA, 'migration-plan')\n        require(_absolute(python) and _absolute(workdir) and callable(secret) and callable(runner)\n                and type(timeout) is int and 0 < timeout <= 3600, 'migration-executor-config')\n        self.plan, self.python, self.workdir = plan, python, workdir\n        self.secret, self.runner, self.timeout = secret, runner, timeout\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def command(python, directory, migration):\n        return (python, '-I', f'{directory}/scripts/migrate.py', 'apply', migration.name, '--yes',\n                *(('--no-transaction',) if migration.concurrent else ()))\n\n    def _materialize(self, index, migration):\n        root = no_symlink(Path(self.workdir))\n        require(os.path.lexists(root) and stat.S_ISDIR(os.lstat(root).st_mode), 'migration-workdir-missing')\n        directory = root / f'{index:02d}-{self.plan.digest[:16]}'\n        try:\n            directory.mkdir(mode=0o700)  # exclusive: a previous attempt's directory refuses\n        except FileExistsError:\n            raise Refused('migration-workdir-exists') from None\n        (directory / 'scripts').mkdir(mode=0o700)\n        (directory / 'migrations').mkdir(mode=0o700)\n        for path, data in (('scripts/migrate.py', self.plan.executor), ('migrations/' + migration.name, migration.sql)):\n            fd = os.open(directory / path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)\n            with os.fdopen(fd, 'wb') as handle:\n                handle.write(data)\n        return str(directory)\n\n    def apply(self, index, migration):\n        require(migration in self.plan.pending and self.plan.pending[index - 1] is migration, 'migration-not-pending')\n        directory = self._materialize(index, migration)\n        url = self.secret()\n        require(isinstance(url, str) and url.startswith('postgresql://') and '\\n' not in url, 'migration-secret')\n        env = dict(PATH='/usr/bin:/bin', LC_ALL='C', PYTHON_DOTENV_DISABLED='1', MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=url,\n                   PGAPPNAME=f'pastorai-first-transition-{index:02d}', PGCONNECT_TIMEOUT='10')\n        return self.runner(self.command(self.python, directory, migration), env=env, cwd=directory,\n                           timeout=self.timeout)\n\n\nclass FirstTransition:\n    def __init__(self, *, plan, journal, host, database, expected, backup_proof, executor, layout, candidate,\n                 config_digest, clock=time.monotonic, sleep=time.sleep, timeouts=None):\n        for value, kind, code in ((plan, Plan, 'plan'), (journal, Journal, 'journal'),\n                                  (host, ObservedHostContract, 'host'), (database, ReadOnlyDatabase, 'database'),\n                                  (expected, DatabaseExpectation, 'expectation'),\n                                  (executor, MigrationExecutor, 'executor'), (candidate, CandidatePort, 'candidate')):\n            require(isinstance(value, kind), 'transition-' + code + '-missing')\n        require(callable(backup_proof), 'transition-backup-missing')\n        require(callable(layout), 'transition-layout-missing')\n        require(journal.lock_fd is not None and host.j is journal, 'transition-journal')\n        require(executor.plan is plan and candidate.spec.sha == plan.application_sha, 'transition-plan-binding')\n        pending = plan.pending\n        require((len(pending), sum(not m.concurrent for m in pending), sum(m.concurrent for m in pending)) == SHAPE,\n                'transition-release-shape')\n        require(expected.validated().ledger == plan.baseline, 'transition-expectation-baseline')\n        require(isinstance(config_digest, str) and re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{64}', config_digest), 'transition-config')\n        self.t = {**TIMEOUTS, **(timeouts or {})}\n        self.plan, self.j, self.host, self.db, self.expected = plan, journal, host, database, expected\n        self.backup_proof, self.executor, self.layout, self.candidate = backup_proof, executor, layout, candidate\n        self.config_digest, self.clock, self.sleep = config_digest, clock, sleep\n\n    # -- journal helpers -------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def _intent(self, step, **fields):\n        return self.j.append('transition-intent', step=step, **fields)\n\n    def _done(self, step, **fields):\n        return self.j.append('transition-done', step=step, **fields)\n\n    def _open(self, step):\n        \"\"\"Intent without receipt: the outcome is unknown and never retried automatically.\"\"\"\n        return (self.j.last('transition-intent', step) is not None\n                and self.j.last('transition-done', step) is None)\n\n    def _observe(self):\n        return self.db.observe(timeout=self.t['observe_s'])\n\n    def _init(self):\n        init = self.j.last('transition-init')\n        values = dict(plan_digest=self.plan.digest, config_digest=self.config_digest,\n                      baseline_digest=self.expected.baseline_digest, application_sha=self.plan.application_sha,\n                      executor_sha=self.plan.executor_sha, candidate_image=self.candidate.spec.image)\n        if init is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-init', production_ready=False, **values)\n        else:\n            require(all(init.get(k) == v for k, v in values.items()), 'transition-inputs-changed')\n\n    # -- entry points --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def run(self):\n        self._init()\n        require(self.j.last('observed-host-intent', 'legacy-resume') is None, 'transition-legacy-resume-started')\n        require(self.j.last('transition-failed') is None, 'transition-stopped')  # first failure is final\n        try:\n            if self.j.last('ddl-marker') is None:\n                self._baseline()\n                self.host.contain()\n                self._quiesce()\n                self._backup()\n                self._mark_ddl()\n            self._migrate()\n            self._release_layout()\n            return self._a9()\n        except BaseException as exc:\n            if self.j.last('ddl-marker') is not None:\n                self.j.append('transition-failed', code=str(exc) if isinstance(exc, Refused) else 'interrupted',\n                              legacy_resume_allowed=False)\n            raise\n\n    def resume_legacy(self, confirmation, *, allow_queue_drift=False):\n        \"\"\"Pre-DDL only; the contract and the driver's ledger proof re-check everything.\"\"\"\n        require(self.j.last('ddl-marker') is None and not self.j.find('transition-intent'),\n                'post-ddl-resume-forbidden')\n        return self.host.resume_legacy(confirmation, allow_queue_drift=allow_queue_drift)\n\n    # -- pre-DDL ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def _baseline(self):\n        observation = self._observe()\n        require_ddl_free(observation, self.expected)\n        if self.j.last('transition-baseline') is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-baseline', evidence='database-read-only', **summary(observation))\n\n    def _quiet_observation(self):\n        receipt = self.host.assert_contained()\n        observation = self._observe()\n        require_ddl_free(observation, self.expected)\n        require_quiet(observation)\n        return receipt['fingerprint'], receipt['queue_digest'], summary(observation)\n\n    def _quiesce(self):\n        start = self.clock()\n        first = self._quiet_observation()\n        self.sleep(self.t['quiescence_interval_s'])\n        second = self._quiet_observation()\n        require(self.clock() - start <= self.t['quiescence_budget_s'], 'transition-quiescence-unbounded')\n        require(first == second, 'transition-quiescence-changed')\n        self.j.append('transition-quiescent', observations=2, writing_sessions=0, active_leases=0,\n                      host_fingerprint=first[0], queue_digest=first[1], evidence='database-read-only')\n\n    def _backup(self):\n        receipt = self.backup_proof()\n        require(isinstance(receipt, dict), 'clone-receipt-invalid')\n        validate_clone_receipt(receipt, self.plan, self.expected.identity, self.expected.baseline_digest)\n        recorded = self.j.last('transition-backup')\n        if recorded is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-backup', receipt_digest=digest(receipt), restore_verified=True)\n        else:\n            require(recorded['receipt_digest'] == digest(receipt), 'transition-backup-changed')\n        return digest(receipt)\n\n    def _mark_ddl(self):\n        require(self.j.last('transition-quiescent') is not None, 'transition-not-quiescent')\n        # Immediately before the irrevocable marker: contained, read-only baseline, quiet, backup valid.\n        self._quiet_observation()\n        backup = self._backup()\n        self.j.append('ddl-marker', irrevocable=True, pending=[m.name for m in self.plan.pending],\n                      baseline_digest=self.expected.baseline_digest, backup_digest=backup,\n                      legacy_resume_allowed=False)\n\n    # -- DDL ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def _migrate(self):\n        ledger = list(self.plan.baseline)\n        for index, migration in enumerate(self.plan.pending, 1):\n            step = 'migration:' + migration.name\n            if self.j.last('transition-done', step) is not None:\n                ledger.append(migration.name)\n                continue\n            require(self.j.last('transition-intent', step) is None, 'migration-outcome-ambiguous')\n            before = self._observe()\n            require_same_database(before, self.expected)\n            require(list(before['ledger']) == sorted(ledger), 'migration-ledger-not-prefix')\n            require(not before['invalid'] and before['index_builds'] == 0, 'database-ddl-in-progress')\n            require_quiet(before)\n            self.host.assert_contained()\n            self._intent(step, index=index, sql_sha256=migration.sha256, concurrent=migration.concurrent)\n            try:\n                code = self.executor.apply(index, migration)\n            except TimeoutError:\n                code = None\n            after = self._observe()\n            failure = self._migration_failure(migration, code, ledger, after, self.expected)\n            if failure is not None:\n                # Definite only for a transactional rollback with no trace; anything else is ambiguous.\n                definite = (failure == 'migration-failed' and not migration.concurrent\n                            and not after['invalid'] and after['index_builds'] == 0)\n                self.j.append('transition-migration-failed', step=step, code=failure, definite=definite)\n                raise Refused(failure)\n            self._done(step, ledger_digest=after['ledger_digest'])\n            ledger.append(migration.name)\n        final = self._observe()\n        require_same_database(final, self.expected)  # before transition-migrated, layout and A9\n        require(list(final['ledger']) == sorted(m.name for m in self.plan.migrations), 'final-ledger')\n        if self.j.last('transition-migrated') is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-migrated', ledger=len(final['ledger']), catalog=final['catalog'])\n        else:\n            require(self.j.last('transition-migrated')['catalog'] == final['catalog'], 'database-ddl-drift')\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _migration_failure(migration, code, ledger, after, expected):\n        # A ledger read from another (or not read-only/visible) database proves nothing: ambiguous.\n        try:\n            require_same_database(after, expected)\n        except Refused as exc:\n            return str(exc)\n        applied = list(after['ledger']) == sorted([*ledger, migration.name])\n        if code is None:\n            return 'migration-timeout'\n        if code != 0:\n            return 'migration-ambiguous-ledger-without-success' if applied else 'migration-failed'\n        if not applied:\n            return 'migration-ambiguous-exit0-no-ledger'\n        if after['invalid'] or after['index_builds'] or not set(migration.indexes) <= set(after['indexes']):\n            return 'migration-index-invalid'\n        return None\n\n    def _release_layout(self):\n        if self.j.last('transition-done', 'layout') is None:\n            self._intent('layout')\n        files = self.layout()  # exclusive or byte-for-byte verification, on every invocation\n        if self.j.last('transition-done', 'layout') is None:\n            self._done('layout', files=files)\n\n    # -- A9 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def _candidate_states(self, ids):\n        states = self.candidate.inspect(tuple(ids[r] for r in ROLES))\n        result = {role: states[ids[role]] for role in ROLES}\n        for role, state in result.items():\n            check_identity(self.candidate.spec, role, state)\n        return result\n\n    def _held(self, ids, created, backend_started):\n        \"\"\"Consumers never started, legacy contained, support preserved, ingress blocked.\"\"\"\n        states = self._candidate_states(ids)\n        for role in CONSUMERS:\n            check_held(states[role], created[role])\n        if backend_started is None:\n            check_held(states['backend'], created['backend'])\n        else:\n            check_backend_running(states['backend'], backend_started)\n        self.host.assert_contained()\n        return states\n\n    def _a9(self):\n        created = self.j.last('transition-done', 'a9:create')\n        if created is None:\n            require(not self._open('a9:create'), 'candidate-create-ambiguous')\n            self.host.assert_contained()\n            require(self.candidate.project_ids() == (), 'candidate-project-not-empty')\n            write_hold_override(self.candidate.spec)\n            self._intent('a9:create', project=self.candidate.spec.project)\n            self.candidate.create_held()\n            found = self.candidate.project_ids()\n            require(len(found) == 4, 'candidate-create-scope')\n            states = self.candidate.inspect(found)\n            ids = {state['service']: ident for ident, state in states.items()}\n            require(set(ids) == set(ROLES), 'candidate-create-scope')\n            for role in ROLES:\n                check_identity(self.candidate.spec, role, states[ids[role]])\n                check_held(states[ids[role]])\n            created = self._done('a9:create', ids=ids, created={\n                role: dict(started=states[ids[role]]['started'], restart_count=states[ids[role]]['restart_count'])\n                for role in ROLES})\n        ids, snapshot = created['ids'], created['created']\n        require(self.candidate.project_ids() == tuple(sorted(ids.values())), 'candidate-project-changed')\n        started = self.j.last('transition-done', 'a9:start-backend')\n        if started is None:\n            require(not self._open('a9:start-backend'), 'candidate-start-ambiguous')\n            self._held(ids, snapshot, None)\n            self._intent('a9:start-backend', id=ids['backend'])\n            self.candidate.start_backend(ids['backend'])\n            state = self._candidate_states(ids)['backend']\n            check_backend_running(state)\n            started = self._done('a9:start-backend', started=state['started'])\n        self._held(ids, snapshot, started['started'])\n        smoke = self.candidate.smoke(ids['backend'])  # fresh read-only probe on every invocation\n        self._held(ids, snapshot, started['started'])\n        if self.j.last('transition-a9-complete') is None:\n            self.j.append('transition-a9-complete', smoke=smoke, consumers='held', ingress_blocked=True,\n                          a10='not-implemented')\n        return dict(status='a9-backend-smoked', smoke=smoke, consumers='held', ingress_blocked=True,\n                    legacy_resume_allowed=False, a10='not-implemented', production_ready=False)\n\n    # -- recovery --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def recovery(self):\n        \"\"\"Objective classification of the journal; never performs an action.\"\"\"\n        j = self.j\n        open_steps = [e['step'] for e in j.find('transition-intent') if self._open(e['step'])]\n        failed = j.last('transition-failed')\n        if j.last('transition-a9-complete') is not None and failed is None:\n            state = 'a9-complete'\n        elif j.last('ddl-marker') is not None:\n            migrations = [s for s in open_steps if s.startswith('migration:')]\n            if migrations:\n                outcome = j.last('transition-migration-failed', migrations[-1])\n                state = 'ddl-failed' if outcome is not None and outcome['definite'] is True else 'ddl-ambiguous'\n            elif any(s.startswith('a9:') for s in open_steps):\n                state = 'candidate-ambiguous'\n            elif j.last('transition-done', 'layout') is not None and failed is not None:\n                state = 'candidate-failed'\n            else:\n                state = 'post-ddl-failed'\n        elif j.last('observed-host-resumed') is not None:\n            state = 'legacy-resumed'\n        elif j.last('observed-host-intent', 'legacy-resume') is not None:\n            state = 'resume-partial'\n        elif j.last('observed-host-contained') is not None:\n            state = 'contained-pre-ddl'\n        elif j.find('observed-host-intent'):\n            state = 'containment-partial'\n        else:\n            state = 'not-started'\n        return dict(state=state, procedure=PROCEDURES[state], open_steps=open_steps,\n                    legacy_resume_allowed=state in ('contained-pre-ddl', 'resume-partial'),\n                    automatic_undo=False, destructive_retry=False)\n\n\n# -- configuration ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass FirstTransitionConfig:\n    repo: str\n    state_dir: str\n    migration_workdir: str\n    python: str\n    docker: tuple\n    catalog: str\n    identity: str\n    lease_columns: tuple\n    observer_applications: tuple\n    manifest: HostManifest\n    candidate: CandidateSpec\n    package_manifest_sha256: str\n    timeouts: tuple\n    digest: str\n\n\ndef parse_config(data):\n    \"\"\"Public values only: unknown keys (a password, a URL) refuse.\"\"\"\n    require(isinstance(data, dict) and set(data) == CONFIG_KEYS and data['schema'] == CONFIG_SCHEMA, 'config-keys')\n    docker, database, candidate, timeouts = data['docker'], data['database'], data['candidate'], data['timeouts']\n    require(isinstance(docker, dict) and set(docker) == {'binary', 'endpoint', 'config_dir'}, 'config-docker')\n    require(isinstance(database, dict) and set(database) == {\n        'identity', 'catalog', 'lease_columns', 'observer_applications'}, 'config-database')\n    require(isinstance(candidate, dict) and set(candidate) == {\n        'sha', 'image', 'project', 'containers', 'network_name', 'release_root', 'hold_override', 'env_file',\n        'smoke_seconds'}, 'config-candidate')\n    require(isinstance(timeouts, dict) and set(timeouts) <= set(TIMEOUTS)\n            and all(type(v) is int and 0 < v <= 3600 for v in timeouts.values())\n            and timeouts.get('observe_s', TIMEOUTS['observe_s']) <= 30, 'config-timeouts')\n    require(all(_absolute(data[k]) for k in ('repo', 'state_dir', 'migration_workdir', 'python')), 'config-paths')\n    require(isinstance(database['lease_columns'], list) and isinstance(database['observer_applications'], list)\n            and all(isinstance(p, list) for p in database['lease_columns']), 'config-database')\n    manifest = HostManifest.from_dict(data['host'])\n    containers = candidate['containers']\n    require(isinstance(containers, dict) and set(containers) == set(ROLES), 'config-candidate')\n    spec = CandidateSpec(sha=candidate['sha'], image=candidate['image'], project=candidate['project'],\n                         containers=tuple((r, containers[r]) for r in ROLES), network_id=manifest.network_id,\n                         network_name=candidate['network_name'], release_root=candidate['release_root'],\n                         hold_override=candidate['hold_override'], env_file=candidate['env_file'],\n                         daemon_id=manifest.daemon_id, smoke_seconds=candidate['smoke_seconds']).validated()\n    require(spec.sha == APPLICATION_SHA, 'config-candidate-sha')\n    require(isinstance(data['package_manifest_sha256'], str)\n            and re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{64}', data['package_manifest_sha256']), 'config-package')\n    canonical = json.dumps(data, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')).encode()\n    return FirstTransitionConfig(\n        repo=data['repo'], state_dir=data['state_dir'], migration_workdir=data['migration_workdir'],\n        python=data['python'], docker=(docker['binary'], docker['endpoint'], docker['config_dir']),\n        catalog=database['catalog'], identity=database['identity'],\n        lease_columns=tuple(tuple(p) for p in database['lease_columns']) or LEASES,\n        observer_applications=tuple(database['observer_applications']), manifest=manifest, candidate=spec,\n        package_manifest_sha256=data['package_manifest_sha256'], timeouts=tuple(sorted(timeouts.items())),\n        digest=hashlib.sha256(canonical).hexdigest())\n\n\ndef load_config(path):\n    try:\n        data = json.loads(read_regular(path, 64 * 1024))\n    except ValueError:\n        raise Refused('config-invalid-json') from None\n    return parse_config(data)\n\n\ndef assemble(config, *, plan, journal, connect, secret, ingress, writers, backup_proof, popen=None, run=None,\n             clock=time.monotonic, sleep=time.sleep, git=None):\n    \"\"\"Wire real ports from configuration plus injected providers; any absent provider refuses.\n\n    Providers (database connection, secret, ingress/writer bindings, backup\n    receipt) are Phase 3 inputs; nothing is contacted while assembling.\n\n    ``writers.observe()`` returns the number of UNKNOWN writers: sources outside\n    the declared allowed ones. Declared sources are this tool's own observer and\n    migration child and, from the A9 backend start on, the candidate backend of\n    ``config.candidate`` (its project/container name); none of them is an unknown\n    writer. Any other source (legacy service, consumer, foreign client) counts and\n    refuses. A binding that counted the candidate backend would fail closed at A9.\n    \"\"\"\n    require(isinstance(config, FirstTransitionConfig), 'transition-config')\n    for value, code in ((connect, 'database'), (secret, 'secret'), (backup_proof, 'backup')):\n        require(callable(value), 'transition-' + code + '-missing')\n    require(ingress is not None and writers is not None, 'transition-host-bindings-missing')\n    binary, endpoint, config_dir = config.docker\n    database = ReadOnlyDatabase(connect, lease_columns=config.lease_columns,\n                                observer_applications=config.observer_applications)\n    expected = DatabaseExpectation(config.identity, plan.baseline, config.catalog).validated()\n    proof = LedgerProof(database, expected, scope=config.manifest.digest)\n    driver = ObservedHostDriver(config.manifest, ingress=ingress, writers=writers, ledger_proof=proof,\n                                runner=PopenRunner(docker_binary=binary, endpoint=endpoint, config_dir=config_dir,\n                                                   popen=popen, resume=True))\n    host = ObservedHostContract(ObservedHostTransport(driver, **config.manifest.transport_scope()), journal)\n    candidate = CandidatePort(config.candidate, runner=CandidateRunner(\n        config.candidate, docker_binary=binary, endpoint=endpoint, config_dir=config_dir, popen=popen))\n    executor = MigrationExecutor(plan, python=config.python, workdir=config.migration_workdir, secret=secret,\n                                 runner=ProcessRunner(binaries=(config.python,), run=run),\n                                 timeout=dict(config.timeouts).get('migration_s', TIMEOUTS['migration_s']))\n    migrations = [m.name for m in plan.migrations]\n\n    def layout():\n        return write_candidate_release(config.repo, config.candidate, config.manifest, migrations=migrations,\n                                       package_manifest_sha256=config.package_manifest_sha256, git=git)\n    return FirstTransition(plan=plan, journal=journal, host=host, database=database, expected=expected,\n                           backup_proof=backup_proof, executor=executor, layout=layout, candidate=candidate,\n                           config_digest=config.digest, clock=clock, sleep=sleep, timeouts=dict(config.timeouts))\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":16,"oldLines":7,"newStart":16,"newLines":9,"lines":[" 7. candidate release layout ``<release_root>/<sha>`` (first_transition_candidate);"," 8. A9: four candidate containers created held (restart=no, gates closed), ONLY","    the backend started and smoked; consumers proven never started; legacy","-   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout.","+   stopped, support preserved and ingress blocked throughout. The running","+   candidate backend is a declared allowed source for the injected writer","+   binding (see ``assemble``), never an unknown writer."," "," Recovery is objective (``recovery()``), never automatic: no undo, no retry of a"," destructive operation, no legacy resume once the DDL marker exists. A"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VSmTvhkcuoMqdasCu472Nh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYfN5VbbGBME5RNpeBNf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qxxs4yvA7BAfiWMVPiHxW4","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_host_driver.py","old_string":"Every other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are","new_string":"The writer binding reports UNKNOWN writers only: sources outside the declared\nallowed ones (the transition's own observer/migration child and, once A9 starts\nit, the configured candidate backend; see first_transition_orchestrator.assemble).\n\nEvery other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1924,"cache_read_input_tokens":92323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1924},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7c0715d-1aa9-47c4-a1be-b9d449b8e96c","uuid":"9eea9c06-d067-4b16-a3db-9391371ba951","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:31:35.528Z","request_id":"req_011CgYfN53ZXsniojU1dmf7b","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Qxxs4yvA7BAfiWMVPiHxW4":{"file_path":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_host_driver.py","old_string":"Every other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are","new_string":"The writer binding reports UNKNOWN writers only: sources outside the declared\nallowed ones (the transition's own observer/migration child and, once A9 starts\nit, the configured candidate backend; see first_transition_orchestrator.assemble).\n\nEvery other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qxxs4yvA7BAfiWMVPiHxW4","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_host_driver.py has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7c0715d-1aa9-47c4-a1be-b9d449b8e96c","uuid":"6cab7cf3-04a5-4907-9723-9c5c1badf97b","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:31:35.565Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/raniel-linux/.codex/worktrees/fase1-a3-transicao-20261029/PastorAi-1.0/deploy/first_transition_host_driver.py","oldString":"Every other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are","newString":"The writer binding reports UNKNOWN writers only: sources outside the declared\nallowed ones (the transition's own observer/migration child and, once A9 starts\nit, the configured candidate backend; see first_transition_orchestrator.assemble).\n\nEvery other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are","originalFile":"\"\"\"Observation/containment/resume driver behind ObservedHostTransport.\n\n``ObservedHostDriver.request(argv, *, timeout)`` answers the transport's\nsemantic commands from an injected runner plus explicit callbacks:\n\n* inspect-host: pinned daemon, pinned network and the seven pinned containers\n  through restricted ``--format`` stdout projections to Python, plus both ingress entries and the\n  unknown-writer callback;\n* redis-meta: TYPE/PTTL/LLEN/ZCARD on explicit keys via ``redis-cli`` inside the\n  pinned, label-verified Redis container; no KEYS/SCAN/values/auth in argv, and\n  an auth error is a refusal;\n* block-ingress, ``docker update --restart=no``, ``docker kill --signal=TERM``\n  and ``docker wait`` on the four legacy IDs only;\n* resume (``docker start``, ``docker update --restart=always`` on the four\n  legacy IDs and open-ingress through both bound entries) ONLY when a\n  ``ledger_proof`` bound to this manifest is injected: a fresh read-only\n  PostgreSQL proof (identity, exact baseline ledger, catalog; see\n  first_transition_database.LedgerProof) runs inside every resume request,\n  immediately before its effect. Without it, resume refuses before any call.\n\nEvery other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are\ncallback-reported scope-bound answers, not independent proof, and no token or\nboolean stands for a human approval. Docker values are CLI-reported for an\noperator-configured endpoint; nothing here certifies the host or quiescence.\nReal bindings/manifest values are Phase 3 inputs.\n\nThe Docker CLI applies --format client-side; only its restricted stdout\nprojection enters Python/journals. Tests use synthetic data only.\n\nErrors carry fixed codes only; runner output never enters exceptions, logs or\nreceipts. No retry: a timeout or refusal is final for that request. Each\nrequest has a cooperative deadline, checked after injected calls return; per-command output caps are acceptance limits.\nPopenRunner reads at most cap + 1 byte; joining buffers temporarily duplicates\nthat bounded storage (plus Python overhead), so this is not a cap on process RSS; an\ninjected runner's own buffering is its responsibility. Nothing runs at import\nor construction; there is no command-line entry point.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections.abc import Mapping\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport select\nimport subprocess\nimport time\n\nfrom first_transition_adapter import ROLES, digest\nfrom first_transition_host_transport import SUPPORT_ROLES, _ids, host_command\nfrom initial_transition_ops import Refused, require\n\nSCHEMA = 'igreja12.first-transition-host-manifest/1'\nMANIFEST_KEYS = frozenset({'schema', 'daemon_id', 'legacy_project', 'network_id', 'service_ids', 'support_ids',\n                           'processing_keys', 'gate_names'})\nENTRIES = ('external', 'evolution-backend')\nQUEUE_KEYS = ('pastorai:webhooks', 'pastorai:webhooks:processing', 'pastorai:webhooks:dead',\n              'pastorai:webhooks:retry-scheduled')\nREDIS_COMMANDS = ('TYPE', 'PTTL', 'LLEN', 'ZCARD')\nREDIS_TYPES = ('none', 'string', 'list', 'set', 'zset', 'hash', 'stream')\nEFFECTS = ('restart-no', 'term', 'wait')\nRESUME_EFFECTS = ('start', 'restart-always')\n# Acceptance caps (bytes of stdout) per command; also PopenRunner's memory bound.\nLIMITS = dict(info=256, network=1024, inspect=64 * 1024, redis=64, effect=256, wait=16)\nMAX_OUTPUT = 1024 * 1024\n\nHEX64 = re.compile('[0-9a-f]{64}')\nDAEMON = re.compile('[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}|[A-Z0-9]{4}(?::[A-Z0-9]{4}){11}')\nPROJECT = re.compile(r'[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,63}')\nPROCESSING = re.compile(r'pastorai:webhooks:processing:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,80}')\nMANDATORY_GATES = ('ALLOW_REAL_SENDS', 'ASAAS_BILLING_ENABLED', 'BREVO_SEND_MODE', 'BROADCAST_ASYNC_ENABLED')\nNETWORK_NAME = re.compile(r'[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,127}')\nIMAGE = re.compile('sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}')\nSTARTED = re.compile(r'[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}(?:\\.[0-9]{1,9})?(?:Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})')\nSTATUSES = ('created', 'running', 'exited')\nHEALTH = ('starting', 'healthy', 'unhealthy')\nRUNNER_CODES = frozenset({'runner-argv', 'runner-bounds', 'runner-spawn-failed', 'runner-output-oversize',\n                          'runner-close-failed', 'runner-failed', 'runner-pending-cli'})\nPROJECT_LABEL = 'com.docker.compose.project'\nSERVICE_LABEL = 'com.docker.compose.service'\nREVISION_LABEL = 'org.opencontainers.image.revision'\nINFO_ARGV = ('docker', 'info', '--format', '{{json .ID}}')\nNETWORK_TEMPLATE = '[{{json .Id}},{{json .Name}}]'\n\n\ndef _gate_names(names):\n    require(isinstance(names, (list, tuple)) and len(names) == len(MANDATORY_GATES)\n            and all(isinstance(n, str) for n in names) and set(names) == set(MANDATORY_GATES),\n            'manifest-gate-names')\n    return tuple(sorted(names))\n\n\ndef _label(key):\n    # A nil label map prints null and a missing key prints \"\"; both normalize to None.\n    return '{{with .Config.Labels}}{{json (index . \"' + key + '\")}}{{else}}null{{end}}'\n\n\ndef inspect_template(gate_names):\n    \"\"\"One JSON array per container; the trusted Docker CLI filters env by name before stdout.\"\"\"\n    quoted = ' '.join('\"' + name + '\"' for name in _gate_names(gate_names))\n    return ('[{{json .Id}},{{json .Image}},' + ','.join(_label(k) for k in (\n            PROJECT_LABEL, SERVICE_LABEL, REVISION_LABEL)) + ','\n            '{{json .State.Status}},{{json .State.Running}},{{json .State.Paused}},{{json .State.Restarting}},'\n            '{{json .State.ExitCode}},{{json .State.StartedAt}},'\n            '{{with .State.Health}}{{json .Status}}{{else}}null{{end}},'\n            '{{json .RestartCount}},{{json .HostConfig.RestartPolicy.Name}},{{json .HostConfig.NetworkMode}},'\n            '[{{range .Config.Env}}{{if eq (index (split . \"=\") 0) ' + quoted + '}}{{json .}},{{end}}{{end}}null],'\n            '[{{range .Mounts}}[{{json .Type}},{{json .Name}},{{json .Source}},{{json .Destination}},'\n            '{{json .RW}}],{{end}}null],'\n            '[{{range $name, $net := .NetworkSettings.Networks}}[{{json $name}},{{json $net.Aliases}},'\n            '{{json $net.NetworkID}}],{{end}}null]]')\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass HostManifest:\n    \"\"\"Sanitized, immutable scope; unknown keys (e.g. any secret) are refused.\"\"\"\n    daemon_id: str\n    legacy_project: str\n    network_id: str\n    service_ids: tuple\n    support_ids: tuple\n    processing_keys: tuple\n    gate_names: tuple\n    digest: str\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, data):\n        require(isinstance(data, Mapping) and set(data) == MANIFEST_KEYS, 'manifest-keys')\n        require(data['schema'] == SCHEMA, 'manifest-schema')\n        require(isinstance(data['daemon_id'], str) and DAEMON.fullmatch(data['daemon_id']), 'manifest-daemon')\n        require(isinstance(data['legacy_project'], str) and PROJECT.fullmatch(data['legacy_project']),\n                'manifest-project')\n        services, support = data['service_ids'], data['support_ids']\n        require(_ids(services, ROLES) and _ids(support, SUPPORT_ROLES)\n                and not set(services.values()) & set(support.values()), 'manifest-identities')\n        require(isinstance(data['network_id'], str) and HEX64.fullmatch(data['network_id'])\n                and data['network_id'] not in {*services.values(), *support.values()}, 'manifest-network')\n        keys = data['processing_keys']\n        require(isinstance(keys, (list, tuple)) and len(keys) <= 64 and all(isinstance(k, str) and PROCESSING.fullmatch(k) for k in keys)\n                and len(set(keys)) == len(keys), 'manifest-processing-keys')\n        values = dict(daemon_id=data['daemon_id'], legacy_project=data['legacy_project'],\n                      network_id=data['network_id'], service_ids=tuple((r, services[r]) for r in ROLES),\n                      support_ids=tuple((r, support[r]) for r in SUPPORT_ROLES), processing_keys=tuple(keys),\n                      gate_names=_gate_names(data['gate_names']))\n        return cls(**values, digest=digest([SCHEMA, values]))\n\n    def validated(self):\n        require(all(type(v) is tuple for v in (\n            self.service_ids, self.support_ids, self.processing_keys, self.gate_names)), 'manifest-values')\n        ok, canonical = _attempt(type(self).from_dict, {\n            'schema': SCHEMA, 'daemon_id': self.daemon_id, 'legacy_project': self.legacy_project,\n            'network_id': self.network_id, 'service_ids': dict(self.service_ids),\n            'support_ids': dict(self.support_ids), 'processing_keys': self.processing_keys,\n            'gate_names': self.gate_names})\n        require(ok and self == canonical, 'manifest-integrity')\n        return canonical\n\n    def transport_scope(self):\n        return dict(legacy_project=self.legacy_project, network_id=self.network_id,\n                    service_ids=dict(self.service_ids), support_ids=dict(self.support_ids),\n                    processing_keys=self.processing_keys)\n\n\ndef _strict_json(text):\n    def constant(_):\n        raise ValueError('constant')\n    return json.loads(text, parse_constant=constant)\n\n\ndef _lines(out):\n    text = out.decode('utf-8')\n    if not text.endswith('\\n'):\n        raise ValueError('unterminated')\n    return [_strict_json(line) for line in text[:-1].split('\\n')]\n\n\ndef _attempt(function, *args):\n    # The failure is reported after the except block: no exception context can\n    # carry runner output into a later traceback.\n    try:\n        return True, function(*args)\n    except (ValueError, UnicodeDecodeError, RecursionError, TypeError):\n        return False, None\n\n\ndef _tail(value, code):\n    require(isinstance(value, list) and value and value[-1] is None, code)\n    return value[:-1]\n\n\nclass ObservedHostDriver:\n    mode = 'observed-host'\n\n    def __init__(self, manifest, *, runner, ingress, writers, ledger_proof=None):\n        require(isinstance(manifest, HostManifest), 'driver-manifest')\n        manifest = manifest.validated()\n        require(callable(runner), 'driver-runner')\n        require(isinstance(ingress, Mapping) and set(ingress) == set(ENTRIES)\n                and ingress['external'] is not ingress['evolution-backend']\n                and all(self._bound(ingress[e], manifest, e, 'observe', 'block') for e in ENTRIES),\n                'driver-ingress-binding')\n        require(self._bound(writers, manifest, None, 'observe'), 'driver-writer-binding')\n        require(ledger_proof is None or self._bound(ledger_proof, manifest, None, 'prove'), 'driver-ledger-binding')\n        self.manifest, self.runner = manifest, runner\n        self.ingress, self.writers, self.ledger_proof = dict(ingress), writers, ledger_proof\n        self.template = inspect_template(manifest.gate_names)\n        self.roles = {ident: role for role, ident in (*manifest.service_ids, *manifest.support_ids)}\n        self.legacy = tuple(ident for _, ident in manifest.service_ids)\n        self.redis_id = dict(manifest.support_ids)['redis']\n        self.redis_verified = False\n        self.refusals = []  # fixed codes only, for diagnosis; never output\n        self._bindings_fixed = (self.ingress['external'], self.ingress['evolution-backend'], self.writers,\n                                ledger_proof)\n\n    @property\n    def supports_resume(self):\n        # Resume needs the database proof and an opener on both ingress entries.\n        return (self.ledger_proof is not None and self._bound(self.ledger_proof, self.manifest, None, 'prove')\n                and all(self._bound(self.ingress[e], self.manifest, e, 'open') for e in ENTRIES))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _bound(binding, manifest, entry, *methods):\n        return (binding is not None and getattr(binding, 'scope', None) == manifest.digest\n                and (entry is None or getattr(binding, 'entry', None) == entry)\n                and all(callable(getattr(binding, method, None)) for method in methods))\n\n    def transport_scope(self):\n        return self.manifest.transport_scope()\n\n    def request(self, argv, *, timeout):\n        try:\n            self._assert_bindings()\n            result = self._dispatch(argv, timeout)\n            self._assert_bindings()\n            return result\n        except Refused as exc:\n            self.refusals = [*self.refusals[-63:], str(exc)]\n            raise\n\n    def _assert_bindings(self):\n        require(isinstance(self.ingress, dict) and set(self.ingress) == set(ENTRIES), 'driver-ingress-binding')\n        for index, entry in enumerate(ENTRIES):\n            require(self.ingress[entry] is self._bindings_fixed[index]\n                    and self._bound(self.ingress[entry], self.manifest, entry, 'observe', 'block'),\n                    'driver-ingress-binding')\n        require(self.writers is self._bindings_fixed[2]\n                and self._bound(self.writers, self.manifest, None, 'observe'), 'driver-writer-binding')\n        require(self.ledger_proof is self._bindings_fixed[3], 'driver-ledger-binding')\n\n    def _dispatch(self, argv, timeout):\n        require(type(timeout) in (int, float) and 0 < timeout <= 30, 'driver-timeout-bound')\n        require(type(argv) is tuple and argv and all(type(a) is str for a in argv), 'driver-operation-forbidden')\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout\n        if argv == ('inspect-host',):\n            return self._inspect_host(deadline)\n        if argv[0] == 'redis-meta':\n            require(len(argv) == 3 and argv[1] in REDIS_COMMANDS\n                    and argv[2] in QUEUE_KEYS + self.manifest.processing_keys, 'driver-redis-scope')\n            return self._redis_meta(argv[1], argv[2], deadline)\n        if argv == ('block-ingress',):\n            return self._block_ingress(deadline)\n        if argv == ('open-ingress',):\n            require(self.supports_resume, 'driver-operation-forbidden')\n            return self._open_ingress(deadline)\n        for kind in (*EFFECTS, *RESUME_EFFECTS):\n            for ident in self.legacy:\n                if argv == host_command(kind, ident):\n                    require(kind in EFFECTS or self.supports_resume, 'driver-operation-forbidden')\n                    return self._effect(kind, ident, argv, deadline)\n        raise Refused('driver-operation-forbidden')\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _remaining(deadline):\n        remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            raise TimeoutError('driver-timeout')\n        return remaining\n\n    def _run(self, argv, deadline, limit):\n        outcome = None\n        try:\n            result = self.runner(argv, timeout=self._remaining(deadline), max_output=limit)\n        except TimeoutError:\n            outcome = 'timeout'\n        except Refused as exc:\n            outcome = str(exc) if str(exc) in RUNNER_CODES else 'driver-runner-failed'\n        except Exception:\n            outcome = 'driver-runner-failed'\n        if outcome == 'timeout':\n            raise TimeoutError('driver-timeout')\n        require(outcome is None, outcome)\n        require(isinstance(result, tuple) and len(result) == 2 and type(result[0]) is int\n                and type(result[1]) is bytes, 'driver-runner-failed')\n        self._remaining(deadline)\n        self._assert_bindings()\n        require(len(result[1]) <= limit, 'driver-output-oversize')\n        return result\n\n    def _callback(self, binding, method, deadline, entry, code, failed='driver-binding-failed'):\n        require(self._bound(binding, self.manifest, entry, method), code)\n        outcome = None\n        try:\n            value = getattr(binding, method)(self.manifest.digest, timeout=self._remaining(deadline))\n        except TimeoutError:\n            outcome = 'timeout'\n        except Exception:\n            outcome = failed\n        if outcome == 'timeout':\n            raise TimeoutError('driver-timeout')\n        self._remaining(deadline)\n        require(self._bound(binding, self.manifest, entry, method), code)\n        self._assert_bindings()\n        require(outcome is None, outcome)\n        return value\n\n    def _daemon(self, deadline):\n        rc, out = self._run(INFO_ARGV, deadline, LIMITS['info'])\n        require(rc == 0, 'driver-daemon-failed')\n        ok, value = _attempt(_lines, out)\n        require(ok and len(value) == 1 and isinstance(value[0], str) and DAEMON.fullmatch(value[0]),\n                'driver-daemon-malformed')\n        require(value[0] == self.manifest.daemon_id, 'driver-daemon-mismatch')\n\n    def _network(self, deadline):\n        rc, out = self._run(('docker', 'network', 'inspect', '--format', NETWORK_TEMPLATE, self.manifest.network_id),\n                            deadline, LIMITS['network'])\n        require(rc == 0, 'driver-network-failed')\n        ok, value = _attempt(_lines, out)\n        require(ok and len(value) == 1 and isinstance(value[0], list) and len(value[0]) == 2\n                and all(isinstance(v, str) for v in value[0]) and HEX64.fullmatch(value[0][0])\n                and NETWORK_NAME.fullmatch(value[0][1]), 'driver-network-malformed')\n        require(value[0][0] == self.manifest.network_id, 'driver-network-mismatch')\n        return value[0]\n\n    def _ingress(self, deadline):\n        states = {}\n        for entry in ENTRIES:\n            value = self._callback(self.ingress[entry], 'observe', deadline, entry, 'driver-ingress-binding')\n            require(type(value) is str and value in ('blocked', 'open'), 'driver-ingress-shape')\n            states[entry] = value\n        return states\n\n    def _row(self, row, network_name):\n        (ident, image, project, service, revision, status, running, paused, restarting, exit_code, started,\n         health, restarts, policy, mode, gates, mounts, networks) = row\n        labels = [None if value in (None, '') else value for value in (project, service, revision)]\n        require(all(v is None or isinstance(v, str) and len(v) <= 128 for v in labels), 'driver-inspect-labels')\n        require(isinstance(image, str) and IMAGE.fullmatch(image) and type(running) is bool\n                and isinstance(status, str) and status in STATUSES and running == (status == 'running')\n                and paused is False and restarting is False\n                and type(exit_code) is int and 0 <= exit_code <= 255\n                and isinstance(started, str) and STARTED.fullmatch(started)\n                and (health is None or isinstance(health, str) and health in HEALTH)\n                and type(restarts) is int and 0 <= restarts <= 10**6\n                and isinstance(policy, str) and policy in ('always', 'no', '')\n                and isinstance(mode, str) and len(mode) <= 128, 'driver-inspect-state')\n        gates = _tail(gates, 'driver-inspect-gates')\n        names = [g.split('=', 1)[0] if isinstance(g, str) and '=' in g else None for g in gates]\n        require(all(n in self.manifest.gate_names for n in names) and len(set(names)) == len(names)\n                and all(len(g) <= 512 for g in gates), 'driver-inspect-gates')\n        mounts = _tail(mounts, 'driver-inspect-mounts')\n        require(len(mounts) <= 64 and all(\n            isinstance(m, list) and len(m) == 5 and type(m[4]) is bool\n            and all(v is None or isinstance(v, str) and len(v) <= 4096 for v in m[:4]) for m in mounts),\n            'driver-inspect-mounts')\n        networks = _tail(networks, 'driver-inspect-networks')\n        require(len(networks) <= 16 and all(\n            isinstance(n, list) and len(n) == 3 and isinstance(n[0], str) and NETWORK_NAME.fullmatch(n[0])\n            and (n[1] is None or isinstance(n[1], list) and all(isinstance(a, str) for a in n[1]))\n            and isinstance(n[2], str) and HEX64.fullmatch(n[2]) for n in networks)\n            and len({n[0] for n in networks}) == len(networks), 'driver-inspect-networks')\n        require(network_name in {n[0] for n in networks}, 'driver-network-detached')\n        require(any(n[0] == network_name and n[2] == self.manifest.network_id for n in networks),\n                'driver-network-mismatch')\n        # Stable configuration only: attachments by name/ID with configured aliases; IPAM is operational on some engines,\n        # never IP, endpoint, gateway or MAC, which Docker clears on stop.\n        attachments = [[n[0], sorted(n[1] or []), n[2]] for n in sorted(networks, key=lambda n: n[0])]\n        return dict(\n            id=ident, image=image, compose_project=labels[0], compose_service=labels[1], revision=labels[2],\n            started=started, restart_count=restarts, restart_policy=policy or 'no', running=running,\n            exit_code=None if running else exit_code, health=health,\n            gates_digest=digest(['gates', sorted(gates)]),\n            mounts_digest=digest(['mounts', sorted(mounts, key=json.dumps)]),\n            networks_digest=digest(['networks', mode, attachments]))\n\n    def _inspect_host(self, deadline):\n        self.redis_verified = False\n        self._daemon(deadline)\n        network_id, network_name = self._network(deadline)\n        ids = tuple(self.roles)\n        rc, out = self._run(('docker', 'inspect', '--type', 'container', '--format', self.template, *ids),\n                            deadline, LIMITS['inspect'])\n        require(rc == 0, 'driver-inspect-failed')\n        ok, rows = _attempt(_lines, out)\n        require(ok and all(isinstance(r, list) and len(r) == 18 and isinstance(r[0], str) for r in rows),\n                'driver-inspect-malformed')\n        require(len(rows) == len(ids) and {r[0] for r in rows} == set(ids), 'driver-inspect-scope')\n        services, support = {}, {}\n        for row in rows:\n            state, role = self._row(row, network_name), self.roles[row[0]]\n            if role in ROLES:\n                state.pop('health')\n                services[role] = state\n            else:\n                support[role] = {key: state[key] for key in (\n                    'id', 'image', 'compose_project', 'compose_service', 'running', 'restart_policy', 'health',\n                    'networks_digest')}\n        ingress = self._ingress(deadline)\n        writers = self._callback(self.writers, 'observe', deadline, None, 'driver-writer-binding')\n        require(type(writers) is int and 0 <= writers <= 10**6, 'driver-writer-shape')\n        redis = support['redis']\n        self.redis_verified = (redis['compose_project'] == self.manifest.legacy_project\n                               and redis['compose_service'] == 'redis' and redis['running'] is True)\n        return dict(scope_digest=self.manifest.digest,\n                    ingress_blocked=all(v == 'blocked' for v in ingress.values()), unknown_writers=writers,\n                    network_id=network_id, services=services, support=support)\n\n    def _redis_meta(self, command, key, deadline):\n        # Only into the Redis container this driver just verified by label; no auth in argv.\n        require(self.redis_verified, 'driver-redis-unverified')\n        self._daemon(deadline)\n        rc, out = self._run(('docker', 'exec', self.redis_id, 'redis-cli', '--raw', command, key),\n                            deadline, LIMITS['redis'])\n        ok, text = _attempt(bytes.decode, out, 'ascii')\n        require(ok, 'driver-redis-output')\n        require(not text.startswith(('NOAUTH', 'WRONGPASS', 'NOPERM')), 'driver-redis-auth-required')\n        require(rc == 0, 'driver-redis-failed')\n        require(text.endswith('\\n'), 'driver-redis-output')\n        value = text[:-1]\n        if command == 'TYPE':\n            require(value in REDIS_TYPES, 'driver-redis-output')\n            return value\n        require(re.fullmatch('-?[0-9]{1,19}', value), 'driver-redis-output')\n        return int(value)\n\n    def _block_ingress(self, deadline):\n        # Both entries are checked; one blocked entry never stands for the other.\n        for entry, state in self._ingress(deadline).items():\n            if state == 'open':\n                require(self._callback(self.ingress[entry], 'block', deadline, entry,\n                                       'driver-ingress-binding') is True, 'driver-ingress-receipt')\n        require(all(v == 'blocked' for v in self._ingress(deadline).values()), 'driver-ingress-still-open')\n        return True\n\n    def _prove_ledger(self, deadline):\n        # Fresh read-only database proof inside this very request, before its effect.\n        proof = self._callback(self.ledger_proof, 'prove', deadline, None, 'driver-ledger-binding',\n                               'driver-ledger-proof')\n        require(isinstance(proof, dict) and proof.get('scope') == self.manifest.digest\n                and proof.get('read_only') is True and proof.get('ddl_free') is True, 'driver-ledger-proof')\n\n    def _open_ingress(self, deadline):\n        # Internal Evolution->backend first, external last; both must end open.\n        self._prove_ledger(deadline)\n        for entry in reversed(ENTRIES):\n            if self._ingress(deadline)[entry] == 'blocked':\n                require(self._callback(self.ingress[entry], 'open', deadline, entry,\n                                       'driver-ingress-binding') is True, 'driver-ingress-receipt')\n        require(all(v == 'open' for v in self._ingress(deadline).values()), 'driver-ingress-still-blocked')\n        return True\n\n    def _effect(self, kind, ident, argv, deadline):\n        if kind in RESUME_EFFECTS:\n            self._prove_ledger(deadline)\n        self._daemon(deadline)\n        if kind == 'wait':\n            rc, out = self._run(argv, deadline, LIMITS['wait'])\n            ok, text = _attempt(bytes.decode, out, 'ascii')\n            require(ok and rc == 0 and re.fullmatch('[0-9]{1,3}\\n', text), 'driver-wait-receipt')\n            return int(text)\n        rc, out = self._run(argv, deadline, LIMITS['effect'])\n        require(rc == 0 and out == (ident + '\\n').encode(), 'driver-effect-receipt')\n        return True\n\n\nGLOBAL_FLAGS = frozenset({'-H', '--host', '--context', '-c', '--config', '--tls', '--tlsverify', '--tlscacert',\n                          '--tlscert', '--tlskey', '-D', '--debug', '-l', '--log-level'})\nENV = {'LC_ALL': 'C', 'LANG': 'C'}\nABS_PATH = re.compile('/[A-Za-z0-9._/-]{1,255}')\n\n\ndef _absolute(path):\n    return (isinstance(path, str) and ABS_PATH.fullmatch(path) is not None\n            and all(part not in ('', '.', '..') for part in path[1:].split('/')))\n\n\ndef _runner_argv(argv, resume=False):\n    if not (type(argv) is tuple and 2 <= len(argv) <= 32 and argv[0] == 'docker'\n            and all(type(a) is str and 0 < len(a) <= 16384 and '\\x00' not in a for a in argv)):\n        return False\n    if argv == INFO_ARGV:\n        return True\n    if len(argv) == 6 and argv[:5] == ('docker', 'network', 'inspect', '--format', NETWORK_TEMPLATE):\n        return HEX64.fullmatch(argv[5]) is not None\n    if 7 <= len(argv) <= 13 and argv[:6] == (\n            'docker', 'inspect', '--type', 'container', '--format', inspect_template(MANDATORY_GATES)):\n        return all(HEX64.fullmatch(i) for i in argv[6:]) and len(set(argv[6:])) == len(argv[6:])\n    if len(argv) == 7 and argv[:2] == ('docker', 'exec'):\n        return (HEX64.fullmatch(argv[2]) is not None and argv[3:5] == ('redis-cli', '--raw')\n                and argv[5] in REDIS_COMMANDS and (argv[6] in QUEUE_KEYS or PROCESSING.fullmatch(argv[6])))\n    if len(argv) == 4 and argv[:3] in (('docker', 'update', '--restart=no'),\n                                     ('docker', 'kill', '--signal=TERM')):\n        return HEX64.fullmatch(argv[3]) is not None\n    if resume and (len(argv) == 4 and argv[:3] == ('docker', 'update', '--restart=always')\n                   or len(argv) == 3 and argv[:2] == ('docker', 'start')):\n        return HEX64.fullmatch(argv[-1]) is not None\n    return len(argv) == 3 and argv[:2] == ('docker', 'wait') and HEX64.fullmatch(argv[2]) is not None\n\n\nclass PopenRunner:\n    \"\"\"Bounded docker CLI runner for a future authorized operator; never used by tests unmocked.\n\n    The endpoint (``unix://`` socket), docker binary and an operator-provided\n    config directory are explicit; the child gets a minimal environment, so no\n    inherited DOCKER_HOST/DOCKER_CONTEXT/credentials/HOME apply. Only block-A\n    read/containment subcommands are accepted, plus ``start``/``restart=always``\n    by ID only when constructed with ``resume=True``. On timeout, oversize or error it\n    ends only its own CLI process, waits at most ``cleanup_wait`` and never\n    retries; an unreaped CLI is counted, not escalated. Killing the CLI does not\n    undo a request the daemon already received. Compatibility with a real\n    Docker CLI/daemon is unverified here.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, *, docker_binary, endpoint, config_dir, popen=None, cleanup_wait=2.0, chunk=4096,\n                 resume=False):\n        require(_absolute(docker_binary) and docker_binary.endswith('/docker')\n                and isinstance(endpoint, str) and endpoint.startswith('unix://')\n                and _absolute(endpoint[len('unix://'):]) and endpoint.endswith('.sock')\n                and _absolute(config_dir) and (popen is None or callable(popen))\n                and type(cleanup_wait) in (int, float) and 0 < cleanup_wait <= 10\n                and type(chunk) is int and 0 < chunk <= 65536 and type(resume) is bool, 'runner-config')\n        self.resume = resume\n        self.docker_binary, self.endpoint, self.config_dir = docker_binary, endpoint, config_dir\n        self.popen, self.cleanup_wait, self.chunk = popen, cleanup_wait, chunk\n        self.unreaped = 0\n\n    def _allowed(self, argv):\n        return _runner_argv(argv, self.resume)\n\n    def _env(self):\n        return dict(ENV)\n\n    def __call__(self, argv, *, timeout, max_output):\n        require(self.unreaped == 0, 'runner-pending-cli')\n        require(self._allowed(argv), 'runner-argv')\n        require(type(timeout) in (int, float) and 0 < timeout <= 60\n                and type(max_output) is int and 0 < max_output <= MAX_OUTPUT, 'runner-bounds')\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout\n        popen = self.popen or subprocess.Popen  # resolved per call, never at import/construction\n        command = [self.docker_binary, '--config', self.config_dir, '--host', self.endpoint, *argv[1:]]\n        proc = None\n        try:\n            proc = popen(command, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n                         env=self._env(), cwd='/', close_fds=True, shell=False, start_new_session=True)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        require(proc is not None, 'runner-spawn-failed')\n        outcome = 'runner-failed'\n        try:\n            out = self._read(proc, deadline, max_output)\n            rc = proc.wait(timeout=max(deadline - time.monotonic(), 0))\n            outcome = None\n        except (TimeoutError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):\n            outcome = 'timeout'\n        except Refused as exc:\n            outcome = str(exc)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        except BaseException:\n            self._cleanup(proc)\n            raise\n        finally:\n            try:\n                proc.stdout.close()\n            except Exception:\n                if outcome is None:\n                    outcome = 'runner-close-failed'\n        if outcome is None and time.monotonic() > deadline:\n            outcome = 'timeout'\n        if outcome is not None:\n            self._cleanup(proc)\n            if outcome == 'timeout':\n                raise TimeoutError('runner-timeout')\n            raise Refused(outcome)\n        return rc, out\n\n    def _read(self, proc, deadline, limit):\n        fd, chunks, size = proc.stdout.fileno(), [], 0\n        while True:\n            remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()\n            if remaining <= 0 or not select.select([fd], [], [], remaining)[0]:\n                raise TimeoutError('runner-timeout')\n            chunk = os.read(fd, min(self.chunk, limit + 1 - size))\n            if not chunk:\n                return b''.join(chunks)\n            size += len(chunk)\n            chunks.append(chunk)\n            require(size <= limit, 'runner-output-oversize')\n\n    def _cleanup(self, proc):\n        # Ends only this runner's own CLI child; never a container, never a retry.\n        try:\n            if proc.poll() is None:\n                proc.kill()\n            proc.wait(timeout=self.cleanup_wait)\n        except Exception:\n            self.unreaped += 1\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":18,"oldLines":6,"newStart":18,"newLines":10,"lines":["   first_transition_database.LedgerProof) runs inside every resume request,","   immediately before its effect. Without it, resume refuses before any call."," ","+The writer binding reports UNKNOWN writers only: sources outside the declared","+allowed ones (the transition's own observer/migration child and, once A9 starts","+it, the configured candidate backend; see first_transition_orchestrator.assemble).","+"," Every other operation refuses before any runner call. Ingress/writer values are"," callback-reported scope-bound answers, not independent proof, and no token or"," boolean stands for a human approval. Docker values are CLI-reported for an"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Qxxs4yvA7BAfiWMVPiHxW4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
